   "AreaReportContent_Text1": "A storyteller's script based on historical events, recounting the history of the Jinzhou region in Huanglong.\n \n ...",
   "AreaReportContent_Text10": "What time is it now? Six? It must be six in the morning. The next surgery should start soon. We're gathered in a meeting room on one of the higher floors, but this isn't the time to be picky. A team this size needs at least three Peregrine Falcon ornithopters for evacuation.\n \n...We're down to just 13 doses of atropine. The heat is rising, and keeping the wounded cool is becoming impossible.\n \nWhere are the reinforcements? Where is the air force? HQ! This is a call for immediate support! Coordinates are back to the Tethys System—we need reinforcements!\n \n...At least... evacuate the elders and children...\n \nIt's getting hotter and hotter, and Brandon's team hasn't returned... Calling for reinforcements...\n...\nDon't lose... hope...",
   "AreaReportContent_Text100": "Twistscales\n \nListen. A low whistle, carried on the scrape of friction, approaches from afar. That sphere, draped in hardened scales, bounds and weaves between steep cliff faces.\n\nThis is the Twistscale, one of the most peculiar creatures inhabiting these wilds. Each morning as the mist disperses, it is driven by an ancient and powerful instinct—to collect.\n\nBeneath its heavy scales lies an extraordinarily keen nervous system. As it rolls and crawls, these hidden senses precisely map the size of nearby minerals, the position of fallen fruit, the lie of branches upon the ground. Once it locks onto a target, powerful muscles draw the scales tight, gripping nature's gifts firm and fast. Tireless, the Twistscale rolls without rest until nightfall, as if intent on curling away the entire mountainside.\n\nBut in the harsh wilds, greed exacts a heavy toll.\n\nAs the \"spoils\" wedged between its scales accumulate, the Twistscale can no longer maintain its compact, nimble form. To bear the weight, it must unfurl its limbs. At this moment, the once-swift cliff-runner moves like an aged tortoise through mud, each step laborious, each breath heavy, stopping often, pressing on.\n\nBut the wilds are fraught with danger. Predators lurk in unseen corners, and once a threat is perceived, it curls into a ball at once. With a sharp clatter, its scales snap shut in fright—and the treasures nestled between the seams slip free. A day's labor scatters across the ground.\n\nTypically, the Twistscale remains curled for about ten minutes, then begins to roll slowly until it confirms the danger has passed. Only then does it relax. After a moment's rest, it coils once more and begins gathering its scattered spoils.\n\nShould this occur as the sun descends into the western sky, the Twistscale returns to the safe burrow constructed from Jade Hexahedron, Floral Crest Jade, and tree branches. There, and only there, does it flip onto its belly and spend the night in its most comfortable posture.",
+  "AreaReportContent_Text101": "",
+  "AreaReportContent_Text102": "",
   "AreaReportContent_Text11": "...We have conducted extensive research on Hoochief behaviors, compiled in this book. Below are excerpts from our observations, so that our readers can compare behavioral changes in Hoochiefs before and after exposure to toxic spores, as well as before and after improvements in the biological environment of the Dim Forest.\n \nHoochiefs Not Exposed to Toxic Spores:\nHoochiefs are a patriarchal, pack-oriented species with a strong territorial instinct. The core members of the pack lead them to collaborate in teams to repel any intruders from their domain.\n\nUninfected Hoochiefs can communicate with each other and use simple tools made of stones and sticks.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text12": "Hoochiefs Exposed to Toxic Spores:\nInfected Hoochiefs develop grey eyes and exhibit anxious, erratic behaviors as the toxic spores infiltrate their bodies, resulting in frequent coughing and vomiting. They may also compulsively scratch and tear at their own backs. In the final stage of infection, each violent cough releases a mist of spores, making them highly contagious sources of infection.\n\nInfected Hoochiefs attack any nearby creatures indiscriminately.\n \nHoochiefs After Environmental Improvements in the Dim Forest:\nFollowing improvements to the Dim Forest's biological environment, new cases of Hoochief infections from toxic spores have dropped significantly. Thanks to the intervention of antibodies developed by the Dim Forest exploration team, infections among Hoochiefs have gradually disappeared, ultimately dispelling the darkness that once shrouded the Dim Forest.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text13": "The Exiles are not a criminal organization with a unified leadership. Rather, the term refers to individuals who reject the control of local authorities and roam the wilds. They come from all walks of life and form a diverse, mixed group. While not inherently malicious, they have few qualms about committing illegal acts such as theft or robbery.\n \nTo survive in the harsh, unsheltered wilderness, they make use of scavenged materials and repurpose technology. Each Exile is typically armed with a Tacetite Weapon, obtained through illegal means, to defend against the threat of TDs or rival Exile gangs.\n \nJinzhou's stance toward the Exiles is primarily preventative, with security forces deployed in areas frequented by them. For those Exiles without significant offenses, the authorities generally adopt a more lenient approach and sometimes try to persuade them to submit under certain conditions. However, for Exiles who are recalcitrant and pose a security risk, the authorities are quick to eliminate them without hesitation.\n \nGiven the Exiles' long history, it is now difficult to trace when the first true Exile emerged.\n \nThere are numerous reasons why someone might choose to join the Exiles in the wilderness: a thief seeking to escape the Patrollers, a deserter too ashamed to face their comrades, or a Resonator who believes they can protect themselves but refuses to adhere to local laws. To become an Exile, one must first defeat another Exile—whether by taking their life, stealing their Ring, or seizing it by force, a symbol of severance from mainstream society. That is how an Exile earns recognition from their peers.",
@@ -7533,7 +7670,7 @@
   "AreaReportContent_Text63": "The mountains crumbled as the iron star fell.\nBeneath its wreckage, there we stood.\nNo more fruit upon the trees, no more fires for the night.\n \nO Sun and stars, you answered us no more.\nO clouds and night, you wept in silent tears.\n \nIn the hush of a lightless night,\nAcross frostlands stripped of warmth,\n \nOnly the Giant, blazing like the sun, remained.\nOnly the Giant, blazing like the sun, remained.\n \n\"Keep living,\"\nSo It said.\n \n—An excerpt from the Royan folksong <i>For the Giant Was Here</i>\n \nAccording to Royan myth and surviving historical records, before the Lament fell upon Lahai-Roi, the Roya lived on the surface, amidst the fjord forests. But in the aftermath of the Lament, Solaris's ▇▇▇▇▇▇ underwent significant changes. Temperatures plunged, followed by the fall of ▇▇▇▇ and ▇▇▇. \n\nThe Roya of that era could only take refuge within the remains of the ▇▇▇▇, wandering the desolate frostlands in search of life upon newly snow-covered plains.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text64": "A pillar of colorful light, a rainbow undone.\nFingertips, hands, and shoulders...\nMother faded like candlelight.\n \nA dark land, the sinking plains.\nBroken wood, shattered ice, wind, and snow...\nWe fell like lemmings into the end.\n \nThe Giant and ▇▇▇▇▇ at war—\nThe end of the plains, the end of the Old Epoch.\n \nDarkness descended,\nIt was the roar of ▇▇▇▇▇.\n \nThe sun ascended,\nIt was the Giant's beating heart.\n \nHow could the rainbow light be extinguished?\nHow could the darkness withdraw?\nHow could we have survived?\n \nFor the Giant was here.\nFor the Giant was here.\nFor the Giant was here.\n \n—An excerpt from the Royan folksong <i>For the Giant Was Here</i>\n \nDespite their struggle for survival in the frostlands, the Roya found no peace. Instead, they faced the first Void Storm in their recorded history. Royan chronicles tell of a blinding radiance that pierced the ice and speared the sky. Everything touched by that storm was consumed, stripped of substance, and erased from the world.\n \nIt was this calamity that triggered the unprecedented collapse of the frostlands, catapulting the ancestors of the Roya into a vast, subterranean cavern. Yet within that endless darkness, a rumbling Reactor Drive rose like a new dawn, for the Exostrider had plucked its own Core and set it alight to become the sun of this underworld.\n \nAs for ▇▇▇▇▇, the foe who once waged war against the Exostrider, the ancient records offer only fragments. Perhaps, to the Roya, the terror of their enemy mattered less than the sacrifice of the one who shielded them.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text65": "[00:02:11]\nAncient Royan folktales suggest that ██ originates from a place deeper than Lahai-Roi itself.\n\nAccording to legend, it's the root of all disasters in the region, located directly beneath what is now Sundermere.\n\n[00:03:49]\nThe Black Shore's monitoring records confirm an anomalous, dual-source frequency signature for ██:\nPoint A: Lahai-Roi, the site of periodically emerging ████ zones.\nPoint B: The Sundermere lakebed, emitting a faint, heavily distorted signal.\n \n[00:05:02]\nThe expedition team followed the signal to the lakebed and discovered a ███ structure, its form resembling ████.\nThe ██ hangs inverted, connected by ███. Its main body is rooted deep into the ground.\n██ extends toward an upper geological stratum, likely oriented toward Bjartr Woods.\n \n[00:05:44]\n▇▇ material is consistent with that of the Exostrider. Surface patterns show distinct ▇▇ characteristics, as though intended to ▇▇ some presence.\nEnergy from the Reactor Drive flows through the ███, continuously feeding and sustaining whatever lies within ██. This appears to maintain a sealed system.\n \n[00:06:22]\nTethys confirms the faint ██ frequency originates from beyond ██.\nThe Research Institute has proposed several hypotheses. The prevailing theory suggests:\nBeneath ▇▇ lies a ▇▇ that bridges ▇▇▇▇. ▇▇ exists to sever that connection.\n▇▇ only seals part of ██; the remainder disperses toward Lahai-Roi, persisting as Void Storms and ▇▇▇.\n \n[00:07:01]\nIf ▇▇ is damaged, the now-separated dual-source ██ will converge again, regaining its complete form. That would be… Solaris' ▇▇.\n \n[00:08:33]\nFurther Royan records note that beyond ▇▇ lies the path the Exostrider once traversed. This \"path\" may be a literal ▇▇, linking directly to ▇▇▇▇.\n \n[00:09:10]\nWhat lies beyond the gate?\n▇▇▇? The universe? The Etheric Sea has barred our path upward.\nThis downward route may be the only remaining ▇.\n \n[00:09:45]\nAs above, so below...\nAs ▇ above, so ▇ below...\nAs ▇ above, so ▇ below...\n▇▇▇ above, ▇▇▇ below...\n \n[00:10:00]\nAttention: Project Code \"Sundermere Lakebed - Aleph-1\" is now classified as a restricted zone.\nAny attempt to approach ▇▇ will be treated as active interference with ▇▇.\nWarning: this recording will terminate after the \"▇▇▇\" sound.\n \n[00:10:78]\n…as ▇… ▇▇… as ▇… below… ▇…\n \n[00:10:66]\n…▇… ▇…\n \n[00:10:78]\n…\n \nRecording terminated abnormally.",
-  "AreaReportContent_Text66": "Speaker: Dr. Scott Rabelle\nDuration: 00:42:11\nExcerpt: 00:37:12 - 00:41:56\n \n_______\n \nThe analysis of ███ samples has confirmed that the ███ material is consistent with that of ███. Energy-flow readings from Bjartr Woods indicate that ███ is continuing to receive a sustained \"supply\" through its root-like structures.\n \n(Brief pause. Soft breathing audible.)\n \nIn other words, ███ is ceaselessly ███ the ███ behind ███. What we are seeing is a dynamic equilibrium, a tug of war between balance and imbalance. If this \"supply\" is disrupted, that equilibrium will collapse. The ███ behind ███ will break through and surge into Lahai-Roi. The P.C.–LH–R/0987 Lahai-Roi Interim Research Briefing warns that the condition of the Sentinel Analog is far from optimistic. If we take action now, there may be a sliver of hope. If we do nothing, defeat is certain. The opening of ███ is inevitable. Regardless of when it opens or who opens it, we must be prepared.\n \n(Uneasy murmuring from the audience.)\n \nThe Sentinel unbinding itself through Resonance is not without precedent. And since we have already demonstrated the near-perfect consistency between the Sentinel Analog and a true Sentinel, then artificially inducing Augmented Resonance is our most viable method to push the Sentinel Analog past its natural limits.\n \nEither we actively direct the Sentinel Analog to open ███ and actively confront the ███ beyond it... or we stand by and watch helplessly while ███ shatters ███ and overwhelms us. Obviously, we are left with no other choice.\n \n(Low discussions among attendees.)\n \nI know. It sounds like a reckless gamble. But look around you. You are Solaris’s finest minds. The pioneers of every field. And I believe… the spirit of science has never lived in certainty. It lives in the courage to take that first step into the dark.\n \nThus, we have finalized the plan:\nA unified research initiative centered on Exostrider research, extending into aerospace, biotic resonance, and energy systems. This will not be just another academic project. This is our civilization's initiative to rescue itself.\n \nI hereby announce that the Polar Collective will be renamed the Spacetrek Collective. At the same time, we will establish a new institution in Lahai-Roi: Startorch Academy. It will serve as the forward outpost for ███ research. There, the Roya and scholars from across the world will study the Exostrider's biomechanical nature and cultivate ███ capable of forming Augmented Resonance with the Sentinel Analog.\n \nThrough the Academy, we will research the Analog Sentinel to further our understanding of post-Lament era laws and ultimately break the Etheric Sea's blockade. Together, we will arrive at a deeper space and a more advanced future. And perhaps one day, our findings on the Sentinel Analog can be shared openly, for the benefit of all Solaris.\n \nA student once asked me, \"What is our final destination?\"\n\nI believe the answer is simple. It's not about returning to the stars. It's about reclaiming the courage to look up at the unknown.\n \n(Applause. Faint electrical static.)",
+  "AreaReportContent_Text66": "",
   "AreaReportContent_Text67": "Following multiple rounds of negotiation, the Roya and the Polar Collective reached an agreement to jointly construct scientific facilities around three key sites: the Exostrider's greatsword on the frostlands, Sundermere in the underground cavern, and the Etching Plains.\n \nThe Solisylum provided critical data on the Reactor Drive's operational cycles and Void Storm zone metrics, enabling large-scale infrastructure planning. Concurrently, Royan Shepherds coordinated the Exoswarm in excavation, transport, and logistical support, ensuring the project's continuous advancement.\n \nThrough this cooperation, the Polar Collective completed the first phase of its expansion: the Frostlands Polar Research Outpost, followed by the completion of the Starward Riseway, a massive vertical transport elevator constructed directly on the Exostrider's greatsword.\n \nAt the same time, the New Federation contributed its most advanced spatial-engineering technology to construct the Spacetrek Research Institute. This ring-shaped facility operates within a local low-gravity band, maintaining a stable orbital trajectory to perform continuous scans and deep-range probing of the greatsword left behind by the Exostrider.\n \nBased on extensive non-invasive analysis of the Exostrider and Exoswarm, combined with data provided by the Roya, the Polar Collective has reached the following conclusions:\n \n1. On the Relationship Between the Exostrider and the Sentinel\nThe Exostrider exhibits extremely high biological homology with the Sentinel, yet its functional profile is sharply divergent. It lacks the Sentinel's cognitive capacity for prophetic insight and civilizational guidance.\n \nIts strengths lie instead in specialized combat capabilities, exceptional mobility, and pronounced biomechanical adaptability. From these traits, researchers propose the hypothesis that the Exostrider is a ███ within the ███ system, fulfilling the roles of transportation and warfare. To distinguish the two, the Institute formally designates the Exostrider as a \"Sentinel Analog.\"\n \n2. On the Physical Nature of the Exostrider\nUnder exposure to and catalysis from the Reactor Drive, components detached from the Exostrider's body differentiate into two classes of Exoswarm entities: animal-type and plant-type. These unique lifeforms replace the extinct fauna and flora of Lahai-Roi, stabilizing and supporting its fragile ecosystem. When sufficiently fed or charged, the Exoswarm return to the Exostrider and fuse back into its frame, repairing damaged sections.\n \nHowever, long-term Royan records on the Exoswarm differentiation and generational cycling reveal that this bio-mechanical restoration process is finite. Like human cells, the Exoswarm possess an upper limit to their number of divisions. Over time, regeneration intervals lengthen, the rate of new differentiation decays, and eventually the process will stop completely.\n \nOur projections are even more concerning. Calculations show that the total number of Exoswarm units that have already been reabsorbed, combined with the maximum potential yield from future differentiation, is still insufficient to achieve the Exostrider's complete structural restoration. This indicates a severe, long-term depletion of the Exoswarm population. While a portion of this loss is accounted for by Voidworm predation, a significant volume of missing components remains unaccounted for.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text68": "Supplemental Report: Functional Properties of the Exostrider and Reactor Drive\n \nFurther investigations and energy-level diagnostics conducted within the underground haven of Lahai-Roi confirm that, even in a dormant state, the Exostrider continues to fulfill an instinctive, self-regulating drive to safeguard both the region and the Roya.\n \nSurvey data indicate that not all components detached from the Exostrider differentiate into sentient Exoswarm units. A significant portion instead transmutes into bionic structural formations embedded within the geological strata. Branching and interlocking like vertebrae, these formations are now classified as Subcrust Spines. Distributed uniformly across unstable tectonic zones, they are hypothesized to play a crucial role in maintaining crustal integrity and channeling energy derived from the Reactor Drive.\n \nOn the Relationship Between the Reactor Drive and the Exostrider's Body:\nAdditional analysis reveals that the Exostrider's energy-generating nucleus, the Reactor Drive, and its physical chassis represent two distinct tiers of creation.\n \nThe Reactor Drive demonstrates an autonomous operational capacity, exhibiting an energy profile with near-▇▇-level output potential, clearly placing it among the higher-order constructs of the ▇▇▇ system. Under the irradiation and catalytic influence of the Reactor's light, components from the Exostrider initiate division, proliferation, and restorative metamorphosis before ultimately reuniting with the main body.\n \nHowever, despite its autonomous traits, the Drive maintains a profound link with the Exostrider itself: should the Exostrider undergo a complete \"death,\" its corresponding Reactor Drive will inevitably be extinguished as well. This indicates that the Drive is not a wholly independent power source—it remains dependent on a form of \"vital signal\" emitted by the Exostrider to sustain its activity.\n \nConclusions and Projections:\nCurrent projections suggest that even if all extant and potential Exoswarm units were to complete their return, the Exostrider's restoration would still fall short of its original peak condition.\n \nMoreover, it is indicated that once ▇▇▇'s creations are bound to a Resonator, they can exceed the limitations of their base form. For humanity, this presents a clear directive: any attempt to interface with, communicate with, or harness the power of these ancient constructs depends fundamentally, and perhaps solely, on identifying their rightful Resonator.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text69": "Startorch Academy Student Handbook: Orientation Guide (Excerpt)\n \nStartorch Academy Student Declaration\nBeneath the Startorch, we pledge to carry its flame forward, to stand beside kindred minds, and to push back the frontiers of knowledge. Let every quest for truth be a spark against the long night until it fades. Together, we build a dawn that is ours.\n \nI. Academic Programs\nStartorch Academy follows a \"Two-Year Preparatory Program + Four-Year Specialization Program\" model.\n \na. Preparatory Program (Years 1–2)\nAll students (except Synchronists admitted to Rabelle College) begin with a cross-disciplinary curriculum. You'll cover foundational sciences, humanities, and essential survival skills for life in Lahai-Roi. Your specialized department placement is determined at the end of Year 2, based on your stated interest and academic performance.\n \nSpecial Note: Synchronists within Rabelle College are placed directly into their department upon admission, follow an exclusive training track, and are exempt from the general preparatory coursework.\n \nb. Specialization Program (Years 3–6)\nThis stage is dedicated to cultivating research specialists. You'll be encouraged to join research groups and embrace our \"learning-through-research\" ethos. Outstanding students aiming for a future within the Academy will receive institutional support.\n \nII. Departments\nStartorch Academy is organized around the study of the Exostrider and Lahai-Roi's unique ecology. Its four departments are as follows:\n \na. Rabelle College (Division of Synchronization Training / Division of Ancient Studies)\nFocused on the selection and training of Augmented Resonators, individuals capable of extra-somatic synchronization with the Exostrider. \n \nNamed after Scott Rabelle, inventor of Rabelle's Curve, the college employs rigorous quantitative methods to cultivate qualified Synchronists. Often referred to as the \"Synchronist Department,\" it functions as the Academy's core, its research providing multiple foundational technologies for other fields.\n \nThe college is equipped with a neural-mechanical simulation cockpit constructed from Exostrider components, capable of replicating synchronization load during piloting. Safety-monitoring technology developed here has been translated by the Resonator Nursing Unit into a \"Frequency Therapeutics\" discipline, benefiting the entire campus community.\n \nb. Department of Exostrider Engineering (Division of Resonator-Mech Synchronization / Division of Tactical Development)\nSpecializes in mechanical integration and tactical equipment research. \n \nBy harnessing the self-replicating properties of Exostrider components, this department develops new intelligent machinery, modular weapons, and conducts applied testing in simulated combat environments. It also bears the critical mission of accelerating Exostrider restoration through external part retrieval and cultivation.\n \nc. Department of Voidmatters (Division of Spatial Warping)\nDedicated to the study of spatial anomalies and Voidmatter physics.\n \nIts research into the Exostrider has yielded communication and spatial-anchoring technologies, enabling cross-dimensional tracking and Synchronist vital-sign monitoring.\n \nIts central research theme revolves around decoding the genesis of the Waveworn Phenomenon. By observing regional Void Storms and analyzing similar events globally, it aims to build a reliable disaster early-warning system. For this reason, this department works closely with the Black Shores.\n \nd. Department of Light Energy Sciences (Division of Light Array Engineering / Division of Ecology Conservation)\nCommitted to photonic energy conversion and ecological maintenance.\n \nThe Light Array Engineering division investigates energy transformation and storage mechanisms derived from the Solis Lens Array of the Solisylum, generating the Reactor's light that powers Academy operations.\n \nThe Ecology division, situated within Exo Genesis Labs and closely tied to acoustic-ecological conservation, is informally known as the Agronomy Wing. Through the behavioral study of Exoswarm units, researchers aim to understand Exostrider cognition and its role in reshaping Lahai-Roi's Ecoacoustic system.\n \nIII. Course Overview\n \nGeneral Requirements\na. Lahai-Roi History: Trace the story of this land and the Academy's origins.\nb. Royan Culture: Understand indigenous traditions and society. (Roya students may waive this course and serve as teaching assistants for extra credit.)\nc. Laboratory Protocols: The foundation of research practice and laboratory safety.\nd. Confidentiality Studies: Mastering security regulations essential for completing the six-year program.\n \nFeatured Electives\na. Vehicle Operations Training: Master the essential mobility skills required in Lahai-Roi.\nb. Physical Conditioning: Build a body that can support a rigorous mind. (Required for all Rabelle College students.)\n \n \nSpecialization Course Preview\nCourses for each department are arranged by teaching sector to maximize efficiency.  Rabelle College Synchronists may enroll across all departmental tracks, shaping them into versatile, top-tier scholars. Those who complete this pathway are regarded as paragons of perseverance and intellect.\n \nLet the dawn be our witness, and our will, the torch. Each morning's attendance at the 8 o'clock mark is a daily recommitment to the scientific pursuit.\n \n(This guide is subject to updates. Please always refer to the latest official notices from the Academy.)",
