   "FavorGoods_121102_Title": "Startorch Memory Album",
   "FavorGoods_121103_Content": "A device that generates massive bubbles, nothing extraordinary except for its dreamy design.\nIt looks more like a toy than a weapon.\nDenia uses it to hide Voidmatter inside the bubbles. A small illusion of being able to protect others.\n\n<i>\"To be honest, Aleph-1 never harbored any hostility toward us. It's simply indifferent to all things. Life and hope are insignificant noises for it. Meaningless. That's exactly why it could never understand how the darkness of <te href=750040>Voidspace</te> is filled with color. Those are lights from a cosmic graveyard. Starlight that faded trillions of years ago. Proof that the stars were once there.\"</i>",
   "FavorGoods_121103_Title": "\"Dream Maker\"",
-  "FavorGoods_121201_Content": "This jade pendant was a keepsake given to him the year he was born. The jade itself was nothing precious, and the craftsmanship unremarkable. In a corner of the pendant, two slender characters were carved: Jingran. His parents once gently tied the pendant to his swaddling clothes, gazing at their innocent child with eyes brimming with joy.\n\"Thank goodness, you're finally here. Thank you for coming to this world.\"\nThey gave him the name Ran, or \"burn\", in the hope that he'd blaze like wildfire that never truly dies. They wanted no life of fame or fortune for him. Their only wish was that he would burn on like a spark upon a grassland—unyielding and enduring. That even when cold nights closed in and the wind howled to break him, he would never bow to despair.\nYet now, a distinct crack ran across the center of the white jade. Jingran traced the fracture with his fingertips, his face unreadable. The Lynx Spirit curled nearby seemed far less at ease, its tail flicking restlessly. After a long silence, it finally muttered under its breath: \"Just a fine crack... and you're still hung up on it after all these years?\"",
+  "FavorGoods_121201_Content": "This jade pendant was a keepsake given to him the year he was born. The jade itself was nothing precious, and the craftsmanship unremarkable. In a corner of the pendant, two slender characters were carved: Jingran. His parents once gently tied the pendant to his swaddling clothes, gazing at their innocent child with eyes brimming with joy.\n\"Thank goodness, you're finally here. Thank you for coming to this world.\"\nThey gave him the name Ran, or \"burn,\" in the hope that he'd blaze like wildfire that never truly dies. They wanted no life of fame or fortune for him. Their only wish was that he would burn on like a spark upon a grassland—unyielding and enduring. That even when cold nights closed in and the wind howled to break him, he would never bow to despair.\nYet now, a distinct crack ran across the center of the white jade. Jingran traced the fracture with his fingertips, his face unreadable. The Lynx Spirit curled nearby seemed far less at ease, its tail flicking restlessly. After a long silence, it finally muttered under its breath: \"Just a fine crack... and you're still hung up on it after all these years?\"",
   "FavorGoods_121201_Title": "Old Jade Pendant",
   "FavorGoods_121202_Content": "A worn ledger, its dog-eared pages scrawled with records of monthly expenses:\n3rd: Picked up a bronze mirror with a broken handle at the market. The vendor swore it once belonged to a <te href=850083>Sentinel</te>. Complete hogwash. The pattern caught my eye, though. Thirty Shell Credits. A bargain or a loss TBD.\n5th: Still stuck in the Mirage Realm for the time being. Asked a courier to deliver some cash to the old lady—should be around two thousand. Packed along a packet of dried apricots for the little one.\n7th: Bought three jin of plums. One jin for brewing, one jin for the lynx (little louse didn't even say thanks), and one jin for myself.\n9th: Gambled on rough jade with the folks at the alley entrance. Lost sixty over nothing.\n10th: Lost another forty. Damn.\n12th: Received my share for the sales of \"Mirage Seeker's Tales.\" Didn't they say it was flying off the shelves? How is it only five hundred?\n18th: I won! Came out twenty Shells ahead in the raw jade gambling! Today's a good day. Bought a bowl of sweet fermented rice to celebrate.\n15th: Replaced a window shutter for the shop. Cost twenty. Smashed by that limp-tailed cat. It's paying for it one of these days!\nBalance of This Month: Don't feel like doing the math. It'll just hurt once I see the number.",
   "FavorGoods_121202_Title": "Ledger",
@@ -56751,6 +56869,18 @@
   "FavorGoods_130802_Title": "Dog Collar",
   "FavorGoods_130803_Content": "Pilar's golden cyberhand, one of the few things left of his.\n\nIt didn't fit her own chrome, but selling it never crossed Rebecca's mind. Nobody ever asked if they could take it. All knew the treatment they'd get: a barrel in the face and a boot out the door.",
   "FavorGoods_130803_Title": "Gold Cyberhand",
+  "FavorGoods_131101_Content": "Even a <te href=850083>Sentinel</te> has things She is not particularly good at, like preparing a thank-you gift for the Arbiter with Her own hands.\n\nShe had meant to make it something dignified, but Her mind wandered, and by the time She had gathered Herself, the fluff gathered in Her palm had been shaped into a little fox far too round. It was a far cry from the imposing miniature Sentinel She had first envisioned.\n\nOf course, unlike the fox forms Hsin conjures using Fractal Proliferation, this is only an ordinary handicraft. It cannot move. It cannot speak. And it certainly cannot feel the warmth of being cradled in someone's palm, or pressed close against their chest.\n\n...Truly, it cannot.",
+  "FavorGoods_131101_Title": "Heart-in-Hand Fox",
+  "FavorGoods_131102_Content": "The <te href=270001>Land of Xuanfang</te>'s first <te href=750051>Rafter Kite</te>, crafted by Hsin's own hand.\n\nShe shaped this ingenious mechanical bird in the likeness of Her cherished friend, the <te href=750054>Xuanling Bird</te>, and placed within it the last frequency the Xuanling Bird had left behind. Her wish was that it might still spread its wings and soar across the Land of Xuanfang.\n\nLater, Xuanfang's Artisans modeled their own after its design, and from then on, Rafter Kites gradually found their way into every household, carrying on the work of conveying people's feelings and words. This very first Rafter Kite became the prototype etched into the memory of countless craftsmen, who spent their lives refining their skill, hoping that one day they might recapture the lifelike brilliance of the bird they once beheld.",
+  "FavorGoods_131102_Title": "First Rafter Kite",
+  "FavorGoods_131103_Content": "A special space within the Heart Realms, and the place where Hsin now most often lingers in rest. The flowers and trees, the streams and pools, and the Moon Lanterns flickering within it were all drawn from the sights She once beheld with Her own eyes as She walked the mortal world, and from the hopes and blessings solemnly entrusted to the Sentinel. Hidden here, too, are many old crafts and forgotten cultures now nearly impossible to find... These fragments, fine as motes of dust adrift on the long river of civilization, She gathered one by one, piecing them together into a world where She might find respite.\n\nOnce in a while, a special guest finds their way here. And when they do, when the stream murmurs its ancient tune and the night falls just as it always has, the <te href=850083>Sentinel</te> sets aside the weight of distant affairs. She sits before the lamplight, takes up a plate of pastries, and speaks with Her visitor of things that can only be said in dreams.",
+  "FavorGoods_131103_Title": "Heart's Rest",
+  "FavorGoods_131201_Content": "Upon meeting the Second Seal, Suoming asked him to forge her a mechanical weapon. The Second Seal first proposed twin blades or a sword, arguing that shaping it as a standard weapon first would allow ten thousand variations to flower from its form. But Suoming simply replied: \"An umbrella would be best.\" The Second Seal mused in silence, and at last understood. Against the Evil Miasma that came howling with wind and rain, Huating needed an umbrella to shield its people from the storm.\n\nThus was born the mechanical umbrella that would one day be known as Nine Shadows. Capable of shifting at will into weapons both long and short, it breaks apart into a rain of fine hidden darts to strike distant foes, or unfolds into an impenetrable shield against ferocious assaults. Its hundred mechanisms and thousand transformations stand ready to answer every hardship.",
+  "FavorGoods_131201_Title": "Nine Shadows",
+  "FavorGoods_131202_Content": "Casting the Power of Ten usually demands the target's willing consent and constant focus to maintain. Should Suoming's concentration slacken for even a moment, the borrowed Forte dissolves into nothing. Remarkable as the art is, she rarely found occasion to use it.\n\nThat changed as she bound her heart to the Ten Seals Covenant. With her own hands, she forged ten Vermillion Locks, crafting each from twelve pitch-black columns capped in vermillion red. Nine were cast to match the First through Ninth Seals, and the last one was held in reserve to seal the Evil Miasma itself. Through these locks, she could sustain the power of all nine Seals indefinitely, freed from the old constraints.\n\nYet even as her hands shaped the metal, Suoming harbored a silent hope: that if fate were to tear those nine away from her one day, she would not be the one to let go...",
+  "FavorGoods_131202_Title": "Vermillion Lock",
+  "FavorGoods_131203_Content": "When the Fourth Seal left her family mansion with Suoming, she brought only one heirloom: a hairpin inspired by the intricate design of a Wonder Ball, anchored by a spherical mechanism lock. Once among the prized treasures gifted to her house by <te href=850154>Mengzhou</te>'s dignitaries, she chose it above all else for one simple reason—she felt the Orb Hairpin suited Suoming's red hair best.\n\nFrom that day on, combing Suoming's hair became the Fourth Seal's \"privilege,\" a habit later shared when the Ninth Seal joined their ranks. In tranquil moments when the Evil Miasma relented, the two would dress her hair while sharing stories of the day's events.\n\nEven now, before binding her hair, Suoming places the Vermillion Locks of the Fourth and Ninth Seals upon her dressing table. She speaks to them of all that has transpired, as if they were still by her side, gathering her hair and laughing over the news of the world.",
+  "FavorGoods_131203_Title": "Orb Hairpin",
   "FavorGoods_140201_Content": "Yangyang's blue beret always has a delicate ribbon attached to its brim. It's her signature look, and a precious gift from her mother before she embarked on her journey.   \nTo Yangyang, it symbolizes her mother's blessing and marks the start of her own journey. She holds onto the resolution she made when putting on the ribbon, determined to see it through until the end.",
   "FavorGoods_140201_Title": "Striped Ribbon",
   "FavorGoods_140202_Content": "As Yangyang grew accustomed to the constant presence of Streams, she began to contemplate capturing the fleeting sound of the wind. With the help of Baizhi's modifications and innovative energy conversion technology, a device was created to store the Streams as visual and tangible information. Whether it be the gentle sound of snow falling on a mountain, an untold story, or a poignant moment that brings tears to one's eyes, Yangyang now had the ability to record these realities that her senses were attuned to.",
@@ -56809,7 +56939,7 @@
   "FavorGoods_141301_Title": "Records of Huanglong Tacet Discords",
   "FavorGoods_141302_Content": "A rumor once went around among the common folk: that the pouch Paragon Qingxiao carries is made of some rare and precious material, impervious to fire and water, with a whole world folded away inside. Within it, they said, lie famed swords and antiquities gathered on her travels, along with every manner of talisman confiscated from the wicked she has punished.\nThe truth is far less wondrous. It holds only small things she might want within reach: a folded map of <te href=850154>Mengzhou</te>, a compass, a talisman or two. Before the legend ever started, it was only sewn from a cloth Qingxiao once used to wipe her blade. She had only just set foot on the path of the sword in those days, and she would sit in the moonlight working the cloth over her sword, unwilling to leave so much as a speck on it.",
   "FavorGoods_141302_Title": "Qingxu Pouch of Wonders",
-  "FavorGoods_141303_Content": "A plain red cord strung with beads of jade. Though a gentle Sword Energy has soaked into it, the years have still worn it thin. Common things of shadow and malice give it a wide berth on sight. By an old tradition of <te href=850093>Huanglong</te>, elders would tie such a charm on a child to ward off evil and call down blessing, so that the child's life might run safe and smooth.\n\nQingxiao has kept this cord all along, in memory of the one thread of worldly attachment left to her in this life.",
+  "FavorGoods_141303_Content": "A plain red cord strung with beads of jade. Though gentle Sword Energy has soaked into it, the years have still worn it thin. Common things of shadow and malice give it a wide berth on sight. By an old tradition of <te href=850093>Huanglong</te>, elders would tie such a charm on a child to ward off evil and call down blessing, so that the child's life might run safe and smooth.\n\nQingxiao has kept this cord all along, in memory of the one thread of worldly attachment left to her in this life.",
   "FavorGoods_141303_Title": "Peace Cord",
   "FavorGoods_150301_Content": "Verina cherishes her Pioneer Association expedition goggles, remnants of a journey and warm memories like <te href=850133>Starflower</te>. Now useless for danger detection, they hold sentimental value to her.",
   "FavorGoods_150301_Title": "Expedition Goggles",
@@ -57243,6 +57373,30 @@
   "FavorRoleInfo_1308_TalentCertification": "The subject's waveform diagram exhibits elliptical oscillations with a stable Time Domain. No abnormal fluctuation tendencies were observed. Examination results are determined to be within normal parameters. \n \nConclusion: Resonant Criticality is high and subject stability remains robust. No immediate risk of Overclocking. \nNo history of Overclocking; however, the subject exhibits emotional instability. Psychological counseling has shown minimal efficacy.\n \n<i>\"****! In Night City, I'm practically the poster child for mental health!\"</i>\n<i>\"This sample is way too textbook... You sure someone didn't just copy-paste it from a manual?\"</i>",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1308_TalentDoc": "[██ Record Modification Log]\n\nModification Target: Rebecca\nModification Code: RA2██-G\n\nThe subject is identified as a Mutant-Type Resonator, with the Tacet Mark located on the right shoulder.\n\nForte Manifestation:\nWhen utilizing firearms originating from ██, the subject can enhance the weapons' own ballistic precision and terminal effectiveness. Building upon this foundation, the subject's attacks can neutralize and disrupt the frequency surrounding specific Nightmare Tacet Discords, inflicting additional damage to targets hit.\n\nFirearm Summoning:\nThe subject can summon three specific firearms tailored to different combat scenarios, using her Forte to materialize and dematerialize these weapons. While a weapon is being summoned, its damage output fluctuates in response to the subject's emotional state, suggesting a direct feedback loop between her Forte and the weapon's performance parameters.\n\n<i>\"The subject's frequency sample exhibits up to 97% similarity to the frequency of Nightmare Tacet Discords in the region. It is speculated that the two share a certain correlation.\"</i>\n<i>\"███ intervened. Related research terminated.\"</i>",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1308_TalentName": "Fury-Type Arsenal",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_Birthday": "Unknown",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_CN": "Ju Huahua",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_Country": "Unknown",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_EN": "Suzie Yeung",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_Influence": "Mengzhou City Hall",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_Info": "Sentinel Hsin, guide of Mengzhou's civilization. Deeply emotional and fond of worldly joys, She has long kept the fires of mortal life burning amid the bustle of trade and the shifting of seasons.",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_JP": "Noto Mamiko",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_KO": "So Yeon",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_Sex": "Female",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_TalentCertification": "[Work Log: H001]\nRabelle's Waveform test sample analysis shows a constant Time Domain, with no abnormal fluctuations detected. Examination results are determined to be within normal parameters. \nConclusion: Resonant Criticality exceeds standard range (counter has reached its upper limit and maximum value cannot be confirmed). Stability is determined to be exceptionally high, with no risk of <te href=850073>Overclocking</te>. However, frequency fluctuations show an extremely minor attenuation. For now, it has been recorded as a margin of error, pending re-examination.\n\n\"...No past history of Overclocking either, so no need for psychological... Uh, do I really need to write this part down too?\"\n\n<i>\"...Wait, who told you to run a Rabelle's Test on the <te href=850083>Sentinel</te>?\"</i> <i>\"What else were we supposed to do? It's the only thing we've got right now. Weren't you the one always going on about wanting to study the Sentinel?\"</i>\n<i>\"Yeah, well, at least we got a reading out of it!\"</i>\n<i>\"Actually... are you sure this data is even valid...?\" \"What do you mean?\"</i>\n<i>\"Well... after Lady Hsin read the report, She just smiled and asked, 'Is this closer to what you're used to seeing?'\"</i>\n<i>\"...\"</i>\n<i>\"...Let's hold off on filing this one.\"</i>\n\nAddendum: H001 was conducted as a single interim observation, utilizing existing Resonator equipment and analytical models. As the subject falls outside their intended scope of use,  certain metrics exceeded instrument range, precluding verification of whether the waveform originates from the Sentinel's intrinsic frequency or constitutes an active adjustment of the test output. The Sentinel's structural composition and powers lie far beyond the purview of existing detection systems. Further study will require a dedicated case file...",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_TalentDoc": "[<te href=850154>Mengzhou</te> <te href=260002>Ministry of Sentinel Affairs</te>: Comprehensive Record of the <te href=850083>Sentinel</te>]\n \n...\nAccording to repeated observations by the Ministry of Sentinel Affairs, Sentinel Hsin the Moon Fox's power can divide one into many, proliferating new forms at will. She can command such entities to divide and extend according to their essential nature, along with their consciousness, perception, and constitutive essence, each taking shape as a distinct Fractal Form. Though each Fractal Form maintains its own existence, it remains tethered to the source, sharing sensation across all proliferations, and can ultimately converge back into a single whole.\n\n...It is also known that Hsin the Moon Fox possesses exceptional mastery in the construction of mechanisms. Her grasp of the principles governing interlocking mechanisms far surpasses current-day craftsmanship. By virtue of Her power of Fractal Proliferation, she can extrapolate, reproduce, and even reconstruct existing designs. Her handiwork can be seen behind many of the ingenious devices found throughout Mengzhou City...\n \nHowever, Fractal Proliferation is no mere art of mirroring or replication. When separated from the source, each Fractal Form undergoes its own experience of the world, its perception shifting with all it sees and feels. Over time, even those born of the same origin may ▉▇▇▂...\n \n<i>Ministry of Sentinel Affairs Personnel Annotation</i>\n<i>Current inspections show no irregularities. This record continues to be filed under the old designation, \"Hsin the Moon Fox, Sentinel of Mengzhou.\" Further examination of Her origins is suspended by order of the Intendant until further notice.</i>",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1311_TalentName": "Fractal Proliferation",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_Birthday": "Unknown",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_CN": "Ge Zirui",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_Country": "Mengzhou",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_EN": "Miracle Chance",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_Influence": "Ten Seals Covenant; Mengzhou - Ministry of Sentinel Affairs",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_Info": "Born in Huating, Mengzhou, she founded the Ten Seals Covenant as its Seal Master to liberate her homeland from the Evil Miasma. Later, by the Sentinel's decree, she served as Intendant of the Ministry of Sentinel Affairs, watching over all of Mengzhou.",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_JP": "Okubo Rumi",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_KO": "Son Jeong Min",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_Sex": "Female",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_TalentCertification": "[<te href=850154>Mengzhou</te> <te href=260002>Ministry of Sentinel Affairs</te> - Resonator Archive]\n\n...\nRabelle's Waveform test sample analysis shows an elliptical oscillation pattern and a stable Time Domain, with no anomalous fluctuations. Assessed as normal.\nResonant Criticality: Extremely high. Her frequency holds steady, with no risk of <te href=850073>Overclocking</te> and no prior history of it.\nNote: her frequency output runs somewhat weak, and her Resonance Ability shows signs of gradual decline. Worth keeping an eye on.\n...\n\n<i>\"'Stable'... well, that's hardly news. I don't think I've ever seen Intendant Suoming's mouth so much as twitch, let alone her waveform.\"</i>\n<i>\"You really need to work on that flair for drama... The point is this: 'her Resonance Ability shows signs of gradual decline.' Don't you find that odd?\"</i>\n<i>\"Indeed. This record dates from Intendant Suoming's first days at the Ministry of Sentinel Affairs. It's been so long, could the initial examination have been flawed?\"</i>\n<i>\"Perhaps. But if the records are accurate... how has Intendant Suoming survived for over a century when her Resonance Ability was already fading?\"</i>",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_TalentDoc": "[<te href=850154>Mengzhou</te> <te href=260002>Ministry of Sentinel Affairs</te> - Resonator Archive]\n\n...\nThe art of Frequency-Locking seals a fragment of a target's frequency within a lock. By design, a Covenant demands the subject’s explicit consent, yet should a dying target's consciousness begin to scatter, the bond may be forcibly forged in the moment their will breaks.\nSecuring a frequency grants the wielder access to the subject’s Forte, though diminished in strength. Constrained by physical limits, she can anchor no more than ten frequencies within her body, allowing her to command no more than ten Fortes.\n...\n\n<i>\"So Intendant Suoming can lock in ten different frequencies, and when she opens a Vermillion Lock, she can use part of the locked person's ability?\"</i>\n<i>\"Seems so. Reading a century-old file like this is a real headache... No wonder they had us comb through it again.\"</i>\n<i>\"Say, if Intendant Suoming went to every city's <te href=850083>Sentinel</te> and asked for a bit of frequency, wouldn't she be unstoppable?\"</i>\n<i>\"Don't be silly. The report says only a sliver of frequency can be locked. For something at the level of a Sentinel, what gets sealed in wouldn't even be enough to wield the corresponding authority.\"</i>\n<i>\"Okay, a Sentinel is a stretch. But locking the frequencies of some strong Resonators should work fine, right? Why doesn't Intendant Suoming do that?\"</i>\n<i>\"I suspect she only calls the frequencies held in her locks these days. For her, the only ones she'd ever forge a Covenant with are those nine...\"</i>",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_1312_TalentName": "Power of Ten",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1402_Birthday": "October 11th",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1402_CN": "Jen Zhang",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1402_Country": "Huanglong",
@@ -57577,6 +57731,7 @@
   "FavorRoleInfo_1610_TalentCertification": "The subject's waveform graph shows elliptical fluctuations, with occasional needle-point spikes. Both peak values trend upward, with no abnormal waveforms observed at present.\nResonant Criticality: Lower than the results from previous reports. Stability remains high, but latent risks of <te href=850073>Overclocking</te> warrant attention.\nResonator Yangyang has a prior history of Overclocking.\nMaximum Overclock rating: Moderate.\nThe subject experienced sensory overload on multiple occasions within the <te href=270001>Land of Xuanfang</te>. Irreversible feather growth at the ends of her hair has worsened, and further spread should be watched carefully.\nRegular physical examinations are advised. Psychological counseling is currently deemed unnecessary.",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1610_TalentDoc": "[Resonance Assessment RA2710-G]\nCompared with previous assessments, the Resonance Spectrum Pattern fit remains extremely high. The <te href=850067>Rabelle's Curve</te> shows no significant change, though a steady upward trend is present, ultimately settling into stable oscillation. The result confirms a Natural Resonator classification.\nThe subject can resonate with surrounding air currents and gather them into energy fields. Beyond this, she can condense her Resonance power into \"Azure Plumes,\" which can neutralize and restore the frequencies they contact, as well as erase the Resonance powers and effects imprinted on living and non-living matters.\nAccording to the subject, she received a frequency from the \"Xuanling Bird\"—a Remnant creature from the distant past of the Land of Xuanfang—during an encounter within the Censure Court of Xuanfang Hold. This event reportedly altered her Resonance Ability. However, Resonance assessment reveals no significant change in the subject's source of Forte. We therefore conclude that no secondary mutation has occurred.\n<i>\"Resonating with a Xuanling Bird... It's an intuitive guess, but the data doesn't support it... Your frequency hasn't so much changed as it has been 'completed.' To put it another way, it's like an amnesiac recalling their past. Perhaps this ability has always been yours, and only now have you come to recognize it. That said, this remains speculation.\"  — From a conversation with a medic of <te href=850092>Huaxu Academy</te></i>",
   "FavorRoleInfo_1610_TalentName": "Voices of Azure Plume",
+  "FavorRoleInfo_5065_Info": "An agent of the Ministry of Sentinel Affairs. Tangning was sent undercover to Xuanfang Hold to observe changes in the city and transmit intelligence to Suoming. After a decade in Xuanfang, he has become a natural part of the place and grown genuinely attached to its people.",
   "FavorStory_110201_Content": "Instead of her name, Sanhua is more commonly referred to as \"the <te href=850124>Magistrate's Bodyguard</te>.\"\n\nSanhua is always seen standing silently behind Jinhsi, maintaining an adequate distance. She stands tall and poised, hidden in the periphery of others' gazes, like a sharp blade ready to be unsheathed at any moment.\n\nAlthough the majority of voices opposing Jinhsi have already subsided, there are still a handful of individuals who would attempt to challenge her authority. Because Jinhsi still held the title of <te href=850091>Jinzhou</te>'s <te href=850084>Magistrate</te>, the seemingly blunt and inflexible bodyguard by her side seemed the easier target for pressure. Or so they assumed. \n\nRegardless of how impossible the ill-intended demands sounded, Sanhua can always flawlessly execute them to the utmost perfection. \n\nWith her impeccable time management, sharp intellect, cool under-pressure demeanor, and savvy negotiation skills... even the harshest critics were left stunned.\n\n\nAs the Magistrate's bodyguard, Sanhua handles both unruly daytime guests, and those uninvited guests who lurk in the shadows.\n\nBeing Jinzhou's Magistrate, Jinhsi is a prime target with a high price on her head. Unwelcome guests sought more than just a cup of tea, but they would soon learn their mistake: instead of hot tea, they were met with the razor-sharp blade of her bodyguard. The crimson-eyed bodyguard seemed to possess an uncanny ability to detect lies. Within seconds, she transformed into a fearsome Asura ready to strike. \n\nOne quick slash revealed shivering limbs as severed trouser legs fell in the cold air. This alone was enough to scare off most of the unwanted guests. Naturally, once the blade returned to its sheath, all shadows and shady dealings would be erased. Jinhsi's radiance would remain untainted, free from contamination.\n\n\nBut sometimes, even Sanhua meets surprises in life... \n\n\"Hello. You must be Madam Magistrate's bodyguard?\" \n\nSo asked the strange resonator standing before her, who bears the same beautiful human-shaped frequency as Jinhsi.\n\nHer world was suddenly filled with new ripples.",
   "FavorStory_110201_Title": "The Magistrate's Bodyguard",
   "FavorStory_110202_Content": "Sanhua's story began with the snow.\n\nHer birthplace was destroyed by a <te href=850080>Waveworn</te> disaster, fueled by an unforgiving blizzard and the emergence of deadly <te href=850081>Tacet Discords</te>. \n\nWithin moments, all forms of life were crushed by the anomalous blizzard, only to be reshaped into a colossal TD standing atop the snowy mountain-turned-<te href=850078>Tacet Field</te>. The sight was both awe-inspiring and horrendous, as the entrenched TD loomed over the devastated landscape, both divine and demonic in its presence. It resembled a giant statue of the Asura.\n\nThe <te href=850086>Midnight Rangers</te> did everything in their power to finally defeat the colossal TD. Finally, it collapsed and disintegrated in piercing roars. While cleaning the battlefield, they were shocked to find a frozen infant amidst the wreckage, her body cold and tinted blue.\n\nThe infant was still breathing faintly. \n\nNo one could imagine how she could have survived such a cataclysm, nor did anyone have the time to ponder such thoughts. The Rangers wiped the bloodstains from their hands and carefully lifted her from the rubble. They shouted, \"We found a baby! A survivor! She's alive!\" \n\nTheir excited cries echoed far beyond the frontlines, instilling courage in every soldier and spreading their love for life across the battlefield, a comforting balm for their worn-out spirits. People believed this to be \"a miracle of divine favor\".\n\nSeveral days later, the girl rescued from the depths of hell opened her captivating odd-colored eyes for the first time. Tacet Discords did not take her life, but instead corroded her right eye. The lingering frequencies miraculously reconfigured themselves into a new eye, allowing her, who was born blind, to directly see the frequencies of all things in the world. \n\n— Unbeknownst to everyone back then, it was also a \"Curse of the <te href=850075>Lament</te>\". \nThe curse distorted everything in her eyes into grotesque, eerie, and cacophonous apparitions, disturbing her senses and shattering her perception of existence in the world. She saw no lies, but neither did she ever see light. \n\n\nShe relived that snowy night endlessly, struggling to escape hell only to fall back into it again, until she became an Asura herself. In a way, she was never truly rescued from that battlefield. Her world was a painting of purgatory, and she was doomed to be haunted by the Tacet Discords for the rest of her life, unable to break free.",
