+  "Guide_TGXW_1_1": "Hooray! I finally found you!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_10": "Slow down.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_11": "Slow down. Take your time.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_12": "All right.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_13": "My name is Lisha. I'm charged with supervising and maintaining a new batch of Autopuppets manufactured in the Thousandfold Foundry.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_14": "...Uh, looks like I'm charged with getting them back as well.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_15": "This batch went out of control too?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_16": "Let me guess, this batch went out of control too.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_17": "Huh? Why did you say \"too\"...? Anyway—yes, exactly!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_18": "They've fled into the Sonoro Sphere nearby, in whole batches. What I can't wrap my head around is... what's drawing them there?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_19": "Ahhh! I just updated the data. More Autopuppets have gone berserk... Nineteen now! No no no... Why does the number keep climbing?!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_2": "...Ah, no, I mean, I finally got hold of a qualified Facilitator!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_20": "If it's not too much trouble... could you help me bring them back, along with the Shell Credits they're escorting? Please, please!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_21": "I'll go take a look.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_22": "I'll go take a look.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_23": "You're a lifesaver... I'll find some way to pay you back, I promise! Even if it means I have to use up my entire internship paycheck!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_24": "Location?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_25": "Gotta locate them first.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_26": "Oh, right—my seniors say the roads around here get pretty confusing, and I didn't want you getting lost. So before I messaged you, I already scouted around and pinned down the entrance to the Sonoro Sphere.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_27": "Here, I'm sending you the pin. You can go right over there. It'll save you some time.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_3": "Word is, once you're on it, there's nothing you can't handle.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_4": "Who told you that?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_5": "Who told you that?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_6": "...Anyway, that's not the point. Bottom line—this isn't spam. So please don't block me on WavesLine! (*>﹏<*)′",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_7": "So, there's a new batch of forty-seven Autopuppets escorting Shell Credits, and thirteen of them have strayed off route... they're on the loose and moving fast.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_8": "Ah, sorry, I should introduce myself first. I actually prepared a proper self-introduction...",
+  "Guide_TGXW_1_9": "I went and recounted the puppets just now, and now I've completely blanked on the whole speech...",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_1": "Thank you! The legend is true. There really is nothing you can't handle, {PlayerName}.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_10": "...How do you always guess right? If I were half as clever as you, my mentor wouldn't scold me so much.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_11": "You're right. The Autopuppets escaped when I wasn't the one on duty. Must have been some slip-up in the shift handover.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_12": "I just happened to be nearby, heard the alarm, and rushed over. Well, they passed through my hands once, so I couldn't just turn a blind eye.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_13": "Why didn't you just do what your mentor told you?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_14": "Why didn't you just do what your mentor told you?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_15": "It would've been the easy way out, sure. But I kept thinking... If everyone just waits for the next guy to clean up, like what could've happened in this Autopuppet incident, that'll land the next person down the line in a real bind.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_16": "And then, to keep accidents from happening, they'd put ever more stringent rules in place. But accidents happen, however careful you are, and when they do, all those strict rules would make it harder to handle...",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_17": "...Um, that came out kind of tangled, huh? Anyway, I know what I'm saying. Hahaha... Sorry to ramble, {PlayerName}!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_18": "Besides, just getting those little ones back safe and sound makes me happy enough! And honestly, you're the one who did the heavy lifting. I didn't do much, really. I'm nowhere near as good as my seniors.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_19": "You did very well.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_2": "By the way, could you keep this whole thing between us?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_20": "That's not true. You already are a great Artisan.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_21": "Um—anyway, thank you so much! You're my hero... no, my savior!",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_22": "It's been a great pleasure to meet you, {PlayerName}! ヾ(≧▽≦*)o",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_3": "Why?",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_4": "Why? You deserve the credit.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_5": "I don't want my mentor to find out.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_6": "To be honest... I'm still a novice. I make plenty of blunders. My mentor, the Artisan I trained under, always says I'm all thumbs. But my other colleagues are lovely. They've been so patient teaching me the ropes.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_7": "When this incident happened, my mentor told me to go by the book and report it. Said they'd send people to handle it soon, and that a newbie like me shouldn't try to take everything on myself.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_8": "That doesn't sound right.",
+  "Guide_TGXW_2_9": "Let me guess, you didn't cause this whole mess, did you?",
   "Guide_TSDXT_2_1": "Hello! Welcome to the Jinzhou branch of the Pioneer Association!",
   "Guide_TSDXT_2_10": "Allow me to make a brief introduction.",
   "Guide_TSDXT_2_11": "Our core mission at the Pioneer Association is to push the boundaries of humanity's understanding through exploration. We ignite curiosity and embrace a trailblazing mindset, inviting adventurers from all backgrounds to join us.",
@@ -87312,6 +88000,90 @@
   "Guide_YMJH_2_7": "Dreamwalker, I have a favor to ask. Can you continue to restore those chaotic Memory Zones?",
   "Guide_YMJH_2_8": "Do you need to ask?",
   "Guide_YMJH_2_9": "Sure, as long as you pay me.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_1_1": "Sorry to trouble you. My name is Luojing; I oversee the seal on a certain mechanism within the Simulacrum Nexus of Mengzhou.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_1_2": "For the first time in four hundred and seventy-three days, the seal's readings have strayed from the record.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_1_3": "I checked the monitoring logs. Before and after the anomaly, you were the one one who had any contact with it.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_1_4": "I cannot say what happened, so I would like to consult you in person.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_1_5": "If it isn't too much trouble, please come and see me. I'll send the coordinates shortly.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_1": "You really came... I thought my message would be treated as spam...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_10": "I can sense it. Part of its frequency is missing.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_11": "More precisely, the frequencies that once held the Autopuppets' minds together were stripped away by Suhsin the Inevitable and scattered across a handful of Autopuppets.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_12": "Without that frequency, it is now little more than wreckage, all but beyond repair.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_13": "{PlayerName}, could you help it recover those lost frequencies? I can't bear for it to forget even who it is...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_14": "Once it's done, I'll want to know the truth.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_15": "After all, it has something to do with Suhsin the Inevitable.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_16": "As you should. I'll keep nothing from you. After all, the blame for what it has become rests with me.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_17": "If its frequencies can be recovered... perhaps it will remember itself.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_18": "Luojing's gaze settles on the Autopuppet, his brow faintly furrowed.\nIt is not the look one gives a machine, but the look one gives an old friend still lying ill.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_2": "...Wait, I know that face... You're the Golden-Eyed One.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_3": "I see... No wonder the seal reacted.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_4": "Yeah, it's me.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_5": "So what exactly is this seal you spoke of?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_6": "A study abandoned long ago. I once led it, and watched, with my own eyes, as it spiraled out of control.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_7": "Now, it still lies sealed deep within the mechanism. I hope... it can one day be set free.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_8": "Lady Hsin laid this seal Herself. As an Arbiter, you have surely sensed that it is incomplete.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_2_9": "Indeed.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_1": "Did you hear that?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_10": "Ever since it awoke, all it has longed for is \"battle.\" That is the fate it was born to.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_11": "{PlayerName}, I've heard of your valor. If this is a fate it can never escape, then please, grant it this final, destined battle.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_12": "Sure.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_13": "I'll do my best.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_2": "Hear what?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_3": "Its voice.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_4": "Now that its frequencies are back, it can finally \"speak.\"",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_5": "I've heard it repeat the same word, over and over.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_6": "Can you guess what it is?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_7": "So you really do understand what it says...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_8": "What is it then?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_3_9": "—\"Battle.\"",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_1": "It's over...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_10": "Being of the prototype batch and one of its failures, it was sealed away here, left to be forgotten.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_11": "But how did you know all this?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_12": "Because I witnessed its birth, and I was the one left behind to answer for it.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_13": "Of course, Lady Hsin never asked us to sacrifice ourselves. She simply knew we would make choices, of our own accord.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_14": "Every time I came, I'd hear faint, broken noises. At first, I took them for the mechanism creaking.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_15": "Only later did I realize it was its voice. It never stopped \"thinking.\"",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_16": "To many, an Autopuppet is nothing but a machine. But once it possessed a mind of its own... I, as a so-called \"Celestial,\" could no longer see it as mere machinery.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_17": "So, it's alright now?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_18": "No. The disorder and damage of long years won't be undone by a single battle.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_19": "But at least, it can finally live as \"itself.\"",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_2": "Four hundred and seventy three days.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_20": "I'll take it from here.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_21": "{PlayerName}, I may yet have to call on you again someday...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_22": "Sure. Reach out anytime.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_3": "This day has finally come.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_4": "Thank you, {PlayerName}.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_5": "I saw an Autopuppet like this once.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_6": "It closely resembles the Skywatch Lancer.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_7": "What stands before you is exactly the prototype of the Skywatch Lancer itself.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_8": "Back then, Suhsin the Inevitable stole the Cloud Shuttle blueprints and tried to mass-produce Autopuppets to turn against Xuanfang.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_4_9": "Fortunately, Lady Hsin intervened in time, and Suhsin could not carry Its plan through.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_1": "{PlayerName}, just letting you know all is well.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_10": "To make the results easier to track, I've fitted it with a \"Sparring Count.\" From now on it will tally the bouts itself.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_11": "As a keepsake, I set the starting figure to the number of sparring it has fought since its creation. Every one of those numbers drawn from its own mind-frequency.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_12": "Thank you again.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_13": "I did nothing special.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_14": "Your hard work made this happen.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_15": "Once, I only wanted to right a mistake. But now I understand...",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_16": "What's truly worth doing isn't to erase it, but to give it a reason to go on living.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_17": "So it needs a sparring partner?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_18": "It's a worthy opponent.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_19": "I did nothing special.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_2": "It's regained its stability. No more losing control or harming passersby from a disordered mind-frequency.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_20": "Your hard work made this happen.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_3": "Still, it needs to keep sparring, to refine its own data and settle into its frequency.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_4": "So it needs a sparring partner?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_5": "Exactly. If you can spare the time, spar with it a few more rounds.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_6": "Every bout brings it closer to being whole.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_7": "It's a worthy opponent.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_8": "Word of your help last time has reached many of my old colleagues.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_5_9": "They've offered to help with the upkeep, and brought in more able capable friends besides.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_1": "It's still looking forward to the next sparring.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_2": "If you've got a moment, why not trade a few blows with it?",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_3": "Lately, it lingers a while after each sparring.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_4": "I think... it's \"thinking.\"",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_5": "Its frequency is steadier today than it was yesterday.",
+  "Guide_YPGX_6_6": "Looks like the sparring data really is paying off.",
   "Guide_YXQJCZ_10_1": "Meow!",
   "Guide_YXQJCZ_10_2": "And you are?",
   "Guide_YXQJCZ_10_3": "Are you that white cat from before?",
@@ -91579,9 +92351,9 @@
   "HelpText_100_Title": "Converging Paths",
   "HelpText_101_Content": "1. During the Moon-Chasing Festival, you can increase Popularity via the activities in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color> and <color=#8c7e51>Fair Stalls</color> to make the Moonlit Fair more lively.\n2. Popularity ranges from Level 1 to Level 6.",
   "HelpText_101_Title": "Popularity",
-  "HelpText_102_Content": "1. Build or upgrade stalls to increase Popularity, gain buffs, and unlock Companions.\n2. Building or upgrading stalls requires Funds, which can be earned by completing Wishes in Lodge Wishes.\n3. Stalls can be upgraded multiple times, with higher levels providing greater buffs.\n4. After building a stall, you can participate in the stall's activities and may earn unexpected rewards, with additional daily rewards for Thus Says the Moon, Hsin's Fortuity, and Riddle Twiddle.",
+  "HelpText_102_Content": "",
   "HelpText_102_Title": "Fair Stalls",
-  "HelpText_103_Content": "1. You can spend Preparation Credits and Funds to fulfill people's Wishes in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color>. Each Wish has its own resource cost.\n2. Fulfilling Wishes will earn you Funds and Wish Tags. Setting new records will boost Popularity.\n3. Send the right Companions to fulfill the Wishes in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color>. You can view their detailed stats on the Companions page.",
+  "HelpText_103_Content": "",
   "HelpText_103_Title": "Lodge Wishes",
   "HelpText_104_Content_1": "There is a preferred Companion Stat for each Wish. Selecting your Companions accordingly will earn you a higher score.\nTo boost your Companions' stats, interact with them on the Companions page.",
   "HelpText_104_Content_2": "Preparation Underway: Your Companions act in turn, earning scores based on their stats.\nScoring Rules: Scores fluctuate each round, as your Companions can't always perform at their absolute best. Nevertheless, Companions with higher stats have the potential to earn higher scores.",
@@ -91593,7 +92365,7 @@
   "HelpText_105_Title": "Companions",
   "HelpText_106_Content": "1. You can interact with Companions to boost their stats and Bond Level.\n2. Each Interaction has its own cost of Wish Tags. A higher cost results in greater enhancements.\n3. Complete Wishes in <color=#8c7e51>Lodge Wishes</color> to earn Wish Tags.",
   "HelpText_106_Title": "Interacting with Companions",
-  "HelpText_107_Content": "[About]\nThe Moon-Chasing Festival is a Huanglong traditional festival that features various origin stories, with the most popular being the tale of The Fox and the Moon. On this special night, families and friends come together to admire the moon and make wishes, expressing their hopes for a brighter future.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 17. For the best experience, complete \"Thaw of Eons\" before participating in this event.\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. Help Xiangli Yao prepare for the Moonlit Fair to boost the festival's Popularity.\n2. Increase Popularity by fulfilling Wishes and building stalls.\n3. Invite Companions to assist in preparations by completing the corresponding Side Quests, and earn higher Wish Ratings and Funds.\n4. Achieve the festival goals to claim and redeem rewards.\n5. After the event concludes, unclaimed rewards will remain available for 30 days and will be reissued via Mail when you log in during this period (Note: Rewards that have not been redeemed will not be reissued.)",
+  "HelpText_107_Content": "",
   "HelpText_107_Title": "By Moon's Grace",
   "HelpText_108_Content": "[About]\nArno, a special agent of the Black Shores, is currently looking for help in gathering Surveillance Datasets on the Lament with the promise of generous rewards. Interested individuals are welcome to speak with him.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and complete Main Quest Act VII \"Thaw of Eons.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. During the event, you need to activate challenges across different regions. You can participate in any unlocked challenge as many times as you want.\n2. After the challenge starts, Surveillance Datasets will appear. Try to collect as many Surveillance Datasets as possible within the time limit. Once all existing Datasets are collected, new Datasets will appear. The more Datasets you collect, the better the rewards.\n3. There are various modules available in the challenges. Utilize them strategically to speed up Dataset collection.\n4. If there are any unclaimed rewards after the event ends, they will be automatically sent to your mailbox when you log in again within 30 days.",
   "HelpText_108_Title": "Solaris Weather Forecast",
@@ -91607,7 +92379,7 @@
   "HelpText_115_Title": "Infinite Battle Simulation",
   "HelpText_116_Content": "[About]\nBeneath the starry sky, the Black Shores keeps its endless vigil, calculating the arrival of the Lament.\nBut fear not the unknown—we are born of the stars.\nComplete event quests to earn great rewards.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and arrive at the Black Shores in the main quest \"To the Shore's End.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\nThe event has three phases, each unlocking as you progress through the main quests.\nComplete event quests to earn great rewards.\nIf you have any unclaimed rewards when the event ends, you can log in within 30 days afterward to receive the rewards via mail.\nPlease note that certain content of the event is not available while in Co-op mode. Quest Tracking is not available in certain game scenes.",
   "HelpText_116_Title": "Where Stars Slumber",
-  "HelpText_117_Content": "[Mail Types]\nThere are two types of mail: Starred Mail and Other Mail.\nStarred Mail stays pinned at the top of your mailbox and does not expire. It will not be deleted when you select \"Delete Read Mails.\"\nOther Mail has an expiration date and will be automatically deleted when it expires.\n\n[Mail Storage]\nThe mailbox can store a maximum of 99 mails.\nOnce the limit is reached, the oldest mails without attachments or with claimed attachments will be automatically deleted.\nMake sure to claim your attachments promptly to avoid any loss from expiration and deletion.\"\n\n[Mail Favorites]\nYou can favorite up to 100 mails.\nFavorited mail never expires while it remains favorited, and will not be removed when you use \"Delete Read Mails.\"\nFor some mail with a set validity period, unfavoriting it after that period has ended will delete it automatically at the same time.",
+  "HelpText_117_Content": "[Mail Types]\nThere are two types of mail: Starred Mail and Other Mail.\nStarred Mail stays pinned at the top of your mailbox and does not expire. It will not be deleted when you select \"Delete Read Mails.\"\nOther Mail has an expiration date and will be automatically deleted when it expires.\n\n[Mail Storage]\nThe mailbox can store a maximum of 200 mails.\nOnce the limit is reached, the oldest mails without attachments or with claimed attachments will be automatically deleted.\nMake sure to claim your attachments promptly to avoid any loss from expiration and deletion.\n\n[Mail Favorites]\nYou can favorite up to 100 mails.\nFavorited mail never expires while it remains favorited, and will not be removed when you use \"Delete Read Mails.\"\nFor some mail with a set validity period, unfavoriting it after that period has ended will delete it automatically at the same time.",
   "HelpText_117_Title": "About Mail System",
   "HelpText_118_Content": "[About]\nMaji, the administrator of Jinzhou Lollo Logistics, decides to relaunch the Lollo Campaign. Complete the campaigns to claim your Lollo Stamps—a gift of gratitude from Lollo Logistics.\nLollo Stamps can be exchanged for Lollo Helper special deliveries.\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, you can complete Lollo Campaigns once per day to obtain a set number of Lollo Stamps.\nEach Lollo Stamp can be exchanged for a Lollo Helper special delivery.\nThere are 3 Inventories for the Lollo Helper special deliveries. Once you collect all deliveries in an Inventory, the next Inventory will be unlocked.\nIf you win the Lollo Express special delivery service, you can claim all deliveries in the current Inventory.\nAfter the event ends, the unfinished Lollo Campaigns will not be available, and all the remaining Lollo Stamps will be recycled.",
   "HelpText_118_Title": "Lollo Campaign: Rerun",
@@ -92125,7 +92897,7 @@
   "HelpText_41_Title": "Echo System",
   "HelpText_420_Content": "[About] \nGreen and hazy as they may feel, school days always shine like gems in the river of memory. Those stories drift among the stars, your constant companions through every quiet night. \nAs the New Solar Celebration unfolds, fresh little tales begin to blossom between you and your friends...  \n\n[Eligibility] \nSolve the first riddle with Sigrika in Main Quest \"Gold Suspended in Shadows\" to unlock\n\n[Rules] \nProgress the Main Quest to unlock the events of the corresponding Resonators. Certain conditions are required to unlock some of the events. Complete \"Whispers Between Stars\" to earn exclusive rewards, including Astrites and a Livery.",
   "HelpText_420_Title": "Whispers Between Stars",
-  "HelpText_421_Content": "",
+  "HelpText_421_Content": "[About]\nHsin has arranged a task for Suoming, asking you to join her in recording the sights of the Simulacrum Nexus of Mengzhou. A trip\"down memory lane\" that draws out the long-sealed memories of the Ten Seals Covenant...\n\n[Eligibility]\nComplete Main Quest Chapter IV Act IV \"Simulacrum of the Heart: Epilogue\" to unlock.\n\n[Event Rules]\nExplore areas according to the clues to collect the scattered Chrono Traces.\nCollect all Chrono Traces to receive Astrites and other rewards.\nMore Chrono Traces will be available for collection in other areas in the future.",
   "HelpText_421_Title": "Dimmr Travelogue",
   "HelpText_422_Content": "[About]\nAfter a rift appeared at the entrance of Honami Crossing, many \"castaway\" objects from Lahai-Roi have begun surfacing across Honami. They have been transformed by the Sonoro into things familiar to the Left Behind. Namipon seems to have a way to restore the original messages hidden within these objects… Soon, the distant scenery of Lahai-Roi will unfold before you.\n\n\n[Eligibility]\nComplete Main Quest \"Flowing Starlight in the Iris.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\nOnce the event begins, Namipon will provide a new clue each day about a castaway object. Track down the correct object and uncover its hidden message to earn rewards.",
   "HelpText_422_Title": "Search for It! Bits of Lahai-Roi",
@@ -92272,7 +93044,7 @@
   "HelpText_501_Title": "Where Stars Cascade Down",
   "HelpText_502_Content": "Complete event activities and limited-time tasks to earn Lollo Vouchers and other rewards.\nCollect Lollo Vouchers to reach milestone stages and claim corresponding rewards.",
   "HelpText_502_Title": "Limited-Time Rewards of Where Stars Cascade Down",
-  "HelpText_503_Content": "",
+  "HelpText_503_Content": "[About]\nDuring the event, obtain Moonlit Rings to unlock and claim rewards. Purchase merchandise tagged with <texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity31/CumulativeRecharge/Common/T_TempScoreIcon.T_TempScoreIcon,0.5/> in the <color=#ad893a>Recommended - Lunite Subscription, Bundles - Special Offers, Outfits, Lunite Purchase, etc.</color> sections of the Store to obtain Moonlit Rings.\n\nWhen the Moonlit Path event ends, the Moonlit Rings will expire and will not be converted to other items. After the event ends, any unclaimed event rewards will be reissued via in-game mail if you log in within 30 days. If you fail to log in within 30 days, the rewards will not be reissued. Don't forget to claim them in your in-game mailbox.\n\n[Eligibility]\n- Reach Union Level 5.\n- Or complete the combat trial in the Main Quest \"First Resonance.\"\n- Or access Main Quest Fast Track Event and proceed with the Main Quest until you reach a specific point.\n\n[Rules]\nDuring the event, obtain Moonlit Rings to unlock and claim rewards.\n\nLog in and enter Moonlit Path to claim: Lustrous Tide x1\nObtain 30 Moonlit Rings to claim: Radiant Tide x1\nObtain 88 Moonlit Rings to claim: Motorbike Accessory - Heart Cube\nObtain 198 Moonlit Rings to claim: Forging Tide x2\nObtain 328 Moonlit Rings to claim: Hsin Resonator Accessory - Where Dreams Shine Clear\nObtain 450 Moonlit Rings to claim: 5-star Weapon Supply Chest - Synth Armament x1 (Open to choose one weapon: Laser Shearer, Radiance Cleaver, Phasic Homogenizer, Pulsation Bracer, or Boson Astrolabe)\nObtain 680 Moonlit Rings to claim: Transducer x3\nObtain 980 Moonlit Rings to claim: Stellar Anchor of Memories x1 (Exchanged for Shorekeeper, Carlotta, or Phoebe, or Transducer x8)\nObtain 1600 Moonlit Rings to claim: Cosmetics Set x1 (Full set includes Avatar: Abby Tossing, Sigil: Not Even Close, Custom Accessory: Not Even Close)\nObtain 2200 Moonlit Rings to claim: Collection Item: Cloudview Seat x1\n\n[Note]\n- If you make purchases through any non-in-game channel, such as the official website's top-up center, please log in to the game while the event is ongoing to receive your purchases, as well as the corresponding Moonlit Rings. If you log in after the event ends, you will not receive the corresponding Moonlit Rings.",
   "HelpText_503_Title": "Moonlit Path",
   "HelpText_507_Content": "[Difficulty]\nEach stage comes in Easy and Hard difficulties, which involve 1 and 2 lost Exoswarm respectively.\n\n[Turn Order]\nEasy: Player and 1 Exoswarm take turns to move, and player moves first.\nHard: Player and 2 Exoswarm take turns to move in this order: Player → 1st Exoswarm→ Player → 2nd Exoswarm, repeat.\n\n[Game Rules] \n- Victory Condition: You clear the level when all Exoswarm are completely surrounded  with no way of escaping.\n- Failure Condition: You lose the level when any Exoswarm flees the current frostlands area.\n\n[Requesting Aid]\nYou may choose to accept aid from the herders after failing or resetting a level 3 and 6 times respectively. Once accepted, the herders will place several Shepherd's Staff in the frostlands in advance to make it easier to surround the Exoswarm.\n\nYou may reattempt both Easy and Hard levels after the first clearance.",
   "HelpText_507_Title": "Rein Back! Migration Mayhem!—Easy and Hard Mode Details",
@@ -92293,7 +93065,7 @@
   "HelpText_514_Title": "Wild Card",
   "HelpText_515_Content": "1. The event quests will unlock progressively according to server time.\n2. Certain event quests have specific unlock conditions. Ensure all prerequisites are completed before you can accept them.",
   "HelpText_515_Title": "Event Quests",
-  "HelpText_516_Content": "",
+  "HelpText_516_Content": "During the event, obtain Moonlit Rings to unlock and claim rewards. Purchase merchandise tagged with <texture=/Game/Aki/UI/UIResources/UiActivity/Image/Activity31/CumulativeRecharge/Common/T_TempScoreIcon.T_TempScoreIcon,0.5/> in the <color=#ad893a>Recommended - Lunite Subscription, Bundles - Special Offers, Outfits, Lunite Purchase, etc.</color> sections of the Store to obtain Moonlit Rings.\nWhen the Moonlit Path event ends, the Moonlit Rings will expire and will not be converted to other items.",
   "HelpText_516_Title": "How to Obtain Moonlit Rings",
   "HelpText_517_Content": "Complete Event Objectives to obtain corresponding rewards.",
   "HelpText_517_Title": "TERM-X: Outreach",
@@ -92483,19 +93255,19 @@
   "HelpText_640_Title": "New Voyage Weekly Subscription",
   "HelpText_641_Content": "1. You have the chance to save your progress every 10 waves in \"Nightmare: Last Stand\" for each Resonator. You can resume your saved progress the next time you challenge this stage.\n2. Each Resonator may have only 1 saved game.\n3. Resonator saves will be reset with each major version update.",
   "HelpText_641_Title": "Resonator Saves",
-  "HelpText_642_Content": "[About]\nThe Black Shores has recently opened a new, high-spec simulation realm, and you've been invited to take part in its first official test. Unlike past tests that focused on validating a single ability, this is an open-ended test of ability diversity, a simulated experiment that keeps iterating under layer upon layer of interference. Its core goal is to record and analyze how many different types of Forte perform within a single vessel. Throughout the test, the Tethys System will continuously provide Resonance ability samples of various types for you to use. As the current test progresses, you're free to connect to different types of ability circuits and explore ever richer structures of ability. Every type of ability you bring online opens up new possibilities in future battles....\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\nIn this mode, you fight simulated battles from a top-down side view using Rover: Spectro or Rover: Havoc. Within a stage, Rover can obtain Resonance Factors from different Resonators, granting corresponding special enhancements to their basic skills or strengthening other combat abilities.\nRover can also gain additional Morph Skills through Resonance Factors. Dealing damage to the enemies generates Morph Energy. Once Morph Energy is full, you can summon or transform into the corresponding Resonator and unleash a special skill.\nThe mode features 7 stages of varying difficulty to challenge. Clearing stages unlocks new Resonators and awards Knowledge Modules and Threshold Sigils. By consuming Threshold Sigils, you can obtain a variety of rewards, including Astrite.",
+  "HelpText_642_Content": "[About]\nThe Black Shores has recently opened a new, high-spec simulation realm, and you've been invited to take part in its first official test. Unlike past tests that focused on validating a single ability, this is an open-ended test of ability diversity, a simulated experiment that keeps iterating under layer upon layer of interference. Its core goal is to record and analyze how many different types of Forte perform within a single vessel. Throughout the test, the Tethys System will continuously provide Resonance ability samples of various types for you to use. As the test progresses, you're free to connect to different types of ability circuits and explore ever richer structures of Forte. Every type of Forte you bring online opens up new possibilities in future battles....\n\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n\n[Event Rules]\nIn this mode, you fight simulated battles from a top-down side view using Rover: Spectro or Rover: Havoc. Within a stage, Rover can obtain Resonance Factors of different Resonators, granting corresponding special enhancements to the basic skills or strengthening other combat abilities.\nRover can also gain additional Morph Skills through Resonance Factors. Dealing damage to the enemies generates Morph Energy. Once Morph Energy is full, you can summon or transform into the corresponding Resonator and unleash a special skill.\nThe event features 7 stages of varying difficulty. Clearing stages unlocks new Resonators and awards Knowledge Modules and Threshold Sigils. By consuming Threshold Sigils, you can obtain a variety of rewards, including Astrite.",
   "HelpText_642_Title": "Resonance Sim Realm",
   "HelpText_643_Content": "",
   "HelpText_643_Title": "",
   "HelpText_651_Content": "- In the Gifts of Starpath event, you can accumulate Convenes by participating in Convene events that fall under Reverb Resonator Convene.\n- Reach Convene milestones in Reverb Resonator Convene to unlock rewards of the corresponding tier.\n- After the Gifts of Starpath event ends, any unclaimed event rewards will be reissued via in-game mail if you log in within 30 days. If you fail to log in within 30 days, the rewards will not be reissued. Don't forget to claim them in your in-game mailbox.",
   "HelpText_651_Title": "Gifts of Starpath",
-  "HelpText_652_Content": "",
-  "HelpText_652_Title": "",
+  "HelpText_652_Content": "[About]\nWith Encore's help, the Second Coming of Solaris has built a Wooly Stage for the Cubie Wars. On this stage, the Cubie Warriors will make use of magical items to wage a fierce battle!\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. Once the event begins, access the event page, then head to the Second Coming of Solaris to embark on an adventure.\n2. You can unlock various Cubie Warriors by progressing through levels and challenging different foes.\n3. If you have any unclaimed rewards when the event ends, you can log in within 30 days afterward to claim them in your Mail.\n\n[Instructions]\n1. Rule Summary: Each Round has two phases: Store and Battle. Build your Storybook by buying, placing, and synthesizing Items, and win as many battles as you can before you run out of Retries.\n2. Store: During the Store Phase, use Coins to buy Items, refresh the Store, and lock or sell Items. You receive Coins each round. Buy Items, then drag them onto the Book Page and adjust their position. Items must be fully placed on the Book Page.\n3. Storage Box: Purchased Items you don't want to equip can go in the Storage Box. Items there won't be used in battle.\n4. Synthesis: Some Items can be synthesized. {Cus:Ipt,Touch=Tap PC=Click Gamepad=Press} an Item to view its synthesis recipe. Once the conditions are met, you can manually synthesize it into a higher-quality Item.\n5. Star Effect: Some Items have a Star range. Placing the right type of Item in a Star slot triggers its bonus effect.\n6. Cost: Weapon Items each have a cost, and the cost limit rises as Rounds progress. If your Weapons' total cost exceeds the limit, you can't enter the match.\n7. Auto Battle: Once battle begins, you can't control your character manually — Items in your Storybook attack, defend, heal, or apply status effects automatically based on their cooldowns and trigger conditions. After the battle, review the damage sources and Item triggers, then refine your build by buying, selling, and synthesizing Items.\n8. Victory Conditions: In each battle, whoever depletes the opponent's HP first wins, earning 1 Trophy. Reach the Trophy count required for the current Stage to win the challenge. Losing costs you 1 Retry, and running out of Retries ends the challenge in defeat.",
+  "HelpText_652_Title": "Cubie Wars",
   "HelpText_653_Content": "Limited-time albums are removed once they expire, and the music within them is removed at the same time.\nMusic that has been removed can no longer be played. If a song has been favorited, it will also be removed from your Favorites list.",
   "HelpText_653_Title": "Limited-Time Album",
   "HelpText_654_Content": "[About]\nThe Imitative Sonic Device left by the Court of Savantae can simulate powerful enemies. The Data Set obtained in this battle can be exchanged for various rewards in the Simulation Training Store.\n\n[How to Unclock]\nUnlocking any difficulty level in Tactical Hologram: Calamity will automatically unlock all other challenges up to that same level. Successfully clearing a difficulty level will also grant all first-time completion rewards for the lower difficulty tiers beneath it.",
   "HelpText_654_Title": "Tactical Hologram: Calamity",
-  "HelpText_655_Content": "[About]\nWith peace restored to the Land of Xuanfang, you return once more to the peak where Qingxiao lives. She gave you a seven-string guqin some time ago; this time, she intends to formally teach you to play...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during the Main Quest \"The Wind Before the Storm\" to access this event early (Complete the pre-requisite Quest \"The Nethermancer's Requiem\" for best experience.)\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, one event quest opens each day at 04:00 server time, for a total of 7. Rover can receive Qingxiao's personal instruction at various locations, playing pieces to refine their skill on the guqin and earning the corresponding event rewards.",
+  "HelpText_655_Content": "[About]\nWith peace restored to the Land of Xuanfang, you once again return to the peak where Qingxiao lives. She gave you a seven-string qin some time ago. This time, she intends to formally teach you how to play it...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14 and activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during Main Quest \"The Wind Before the Storm\" to access this event early (Complete the pre-requisite Quest \"The Nethermancer's Requiem\" for the best experience.).\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, one event quest opens each day at 04:00 server time, for a total of 7 quests. You can receive Qingxiao's personal instruction at various locations, play pieces to refine your skill on the guqin, and earn the corresponding event rewards.",
   "HelpText_655_Title": "The Strings Remember",
   "HelpText_65_Content": "[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 14.\n\n[Event Rules]\nDuring the event, you can consume Waveplates to obtain double rewards after completing Simulation Challenges and Forgery Challenges.\nThe double reward attempts are shared between Simulation Challenges and Forgery Challenges.\nPlease refer to Bountiful Crescendo page for the remaining attempts to claim double rewards.",
   "HelpText_65_Title": "About Bountiful Crescendo",
@@ -92516,24 +93288,30 @@
   "HelpText_669_Title": "Stay tuned",
   "HelpText_66_Content": "[Participation Requirement]\nReach Union Level 19.\n\nEvent Rules\nDuring the event, you can consume Waveplates to obtain double rewards after completing Tacet Suppression.\nPlease refer to Chord Cleansing page for the remaining attempts to claim double rewards.",
   "HelpText_66_Title": "Chord Cleansing",
-  "HelpText_670_Content": "[About]\nThe Ivory Gatekeeper has sent you an SOS over WavesLine! The gate in the depths of the Somnoire—the one that should never be opened, the one you once shut—has somehow come open again. Now, terrifying Nightmares are once again running rampant in the Somnoire...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 22. Activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during Main Quest \"The Wind Before the Storm.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. In this challenge, you can choose \"Dorothy's Companions\" as Echoes to assist you in battle, greatly enhancing the combat abilities of Resonators.\n2. Downed Resonators will automatically revive after a while.\n3. This event can be played in Co-Op Mode.\n4. Only designated Echoes can be used in this event (Sonatas remain effective; only the main Echo Skill is replaced).\n5. Surface Layer Stage Points: Clearance Points + (Remaining Time x Time Coefficient).\n6. Clear all Surface Layer stages to unlock the Abyss of the Final Dreams for a boss-rush challenge.\n7. Total Points are the sum of the highest points from the Surface Layer stages and the Abyss of the Final Dreams (Deep Layer stages other than the Abyss of the Final Dreams do not have points).",
+  "HelpText_670_Content": "[About]\nThe Ivory Gatekeeper has sent you an SOS over WavesLine! The gate in the depths of the Somnoire—the one that should never be opened, the one you once shut—has somehow come open again. Now, terrifying Nightmares are once again running rampant in the Somnoire...\n\n[Eligibility]\nReach Union Level 22. Activate the Four Chime Shaftpost during Main Quest \"The Wind Before the Storm.\"\n\n[Event Rules]\n1. In this challenge, you can choose \"Support Echoes\" to assist you in battle, greatly enhancing the combat abilities of Resonators.\n2. Downed Resonators will automatically revive after a while.\n3. This event can be played in Co-Op Mode.\n4. Only designated Echoes can be used in this event (Sonatas remain effective; only the main Echo Skill is replaced).\n5. Surface Layer Stage Points: Clearance Points + (Remaining Time x Time Coefficient).\n6. Clear all Surface Layer stages to unlock the Abyss of the Final Dreams for a boss-rush challenge.\n7. Total Points are the sum of the highest points from the Surface Layer stages and the Abyss of the Final Dreams (Deep Layer stages other than the Abyss of the Final Dreams do not have points).",
   "HelpText_670_Title": "New Event \"If Dreams Still Reverberate\" is now available!",
   "HelpText_676_Content": "Stay tuned",
   "HelpText_676_Title": "Stay tuned",
   "HelpText_677_Content": "Stay tuned",
   "HelpText_677_Title": "Stay tuned",
