   "InfoDisplay_35000102_Title": "Shadowcast Chamber",
   "InfoDisplay_35000103_Text": "\"Countless Autopuppets, swift as Pickets and Jade Nether Serpents, fierce as Fog Lionarchs and Forbidden Bastions, serve as potent weapons against the Tacet Discords.\nThey form the backbone of the Land of Xuanfang's defense, clashing with the Lament on open ground and purging Tacet Discords within Censure Courts.\"",
   "InfoDisplay_35000103_Title": "Shadowcast Chamber",
-  "InfoDisplay_35000104_Text": "\"The Autopuppets in the Land of Xuanfang seem to possess  spirit of their own. It is said Hsin the Moon Fox granted them a trace of sentience, enough to act of their own accord and move without a guiding hand.\"",
+  "InfoDisplay_35000104_Text": "\"The Autopuppets in the Land of Xuanfang seem to possess spirits of their own. It is said Hsin the Moon Fox granted them a trace of sentience, enough to act of their own accord and move without a guiding hand.\"",
   "InfoDisplay_35000104_Title": "Shadowcast Chamber",
   "InfoDisplay_35000105_Text": "Once completed, this chamber will be dedicated exclusively to testing Fogveil Pagoda's transformation functions.\n \nThe following are the construction precautions:\n1. Standard Construction Procedure\n<b>First, design a transformable \"Model Box.\" After confirming its transformation functions are sound, proceed to construct the large-scale Replica Chamber.</b>\n 2. Transformation Standards\n<b>The chamber must correspond one-to-one with the \"Model Box\" When the Model Box transforms, the chamber must undergo the same changes.</b>\n3. ▇▇▇▇▇▇▇▇ \n......\n \nAppendix:\n \nQ-L1NG:\nMaster, we've already finished building three Chambers. It should be perfectly safe by now, right? Why not just start building the rooms directly from here on out? I don't want to keep making Model Boxes. They just sit on the table afterward. We never actually use them...\nT-G0NG:\nA blunt knife wastes more time than a sharp one. If we cut corners now, we will regret it if a Chamber fails. Follow the rules. Design the Model Box first, then build the Chamber.\nQ-L1NG:\nUgh, fine...",
   "InfoDisplay_35000105_Title": "Replica Chamber Regulations",
@@ -99525,17 +100308,33 @@
   "InfoDisplay_36050001_Text": "[Start of Recording]\n...\n\nGentle Female Voice: As you requested, ████ has fallen into isolation.\n\nGentle Female Voice: Nothing stands between you and your plans now, but don't forget our agreement.\n\nStern Male Voice: Sure, ████ is yours.\n\nStern Male Voice: But only after I've obtained the ██ inside of it.\n\nGentle Female Voice: Very well, I'll be waiting.\n\nGentle Female Voice: So it seems... you are no different from the Court of Savantae after all.\n\n...\n\n[End of Recording]",
   "InfoDisplay_36050001_Title": "A Damaged Communication Log",
   "InfoDisplay_36050002_Text": "Sample █-034\nConsciousness incomplete. Memory fragmented. Body exhibits uncontrollable tremors.\nHypothesis: Selecting Reverberations with less frequency decay may yield better results.\nStatus: Disposed\n...\n\nSample █-145\nConsciousness relatively intact. Retains basic biographical memory, but cannot maintain autonomous control of the body.\nHypothesis: Willpower too feeble for proper fusion with the Autopuppet kernel.\nStatus: Disposed\n...\n\nSample █-215\nReverberation sourced from a Resonator. Consciousness clear. Minor memory loss. Activity ceased minutes after initiation.\nSuspect emotional severance was incomplete. Sample displayed irrational self-destructive behavior.\nStatus: Disposed\n...\n\nI need more time... Too many mysteries still unsolved.\nCould it be that the Reverberations of mere mortals are simply incapable of reaching the journey's end?",
-  "InfoDisplay_36050002_Title": "Damaged Experiment Note I",
+  "InfoDisplay_36050002_Title": "Damaged Experiment Note II",
   "InfoDisplay_36050003_Text": "I never imagined a mere glimpse at the the ██'s knowledge could yield such fresh insights.\n\nSo this is how the so-called ████ of civilizations perceives Solaris.\n\n...\n\nNo more need to hunt down those Reverberations soaked in gentle emotion just to serve as a base for the ██.\n\nThe intensity of emotion carried by the Reverberations no longer matters. Strip them away completely, and we can mass-produce ideal materials. Though this calls for further experimentation.\n\n...\n\nBefore, I'd have to splice several Reverberations together and blend their frequencies to facilitate the ██ between the Reverberations and the Autopuppet kernels.\n\nNow? A single Reverberation achieves a ██ efficiency several times greater.\n\nIf I push it further... I might even be able to anchor only a single consciousness within the Autopuppet kernel.\n\n...Fascinating.",
-  "InfoDisplay_36050003_Title": "Damaged Experiment Note II",
+  "InfoDisplay_36050003_Title": "Damaged Experiment Note I",
   "InfoDisplay_36050004_Text": "...\n\nThe beacon fires of the Fortress and Gorges War at last burned low, and peace was restored across the realms.\n\nMingting issued a proclamation, calling upon the full might of Huanglong to raise a new fortified city south of the Central Plains and naming it Jinzhou. Thenceforth, the lands east of the Mountains of Spirits and south of the Norfall Barrens fell under Jinzhou's jurisdiction.\n\nThe first Magistrate of Jinzhou decreed that the city would bear no emblem of its own. Instead, it would share the insignia of Huanglong, in remembrance of the bond forged in aid with the one capital and five cities.\n\n...",
   "InfoDisplay_36050004_Title": "News Highlight of the New City (Excerpt)",
-  "InfoDisplay_36050005_Text": "(There's messy handwriting crammed into the margins, seemingly added bit by bit over time.)\n\nShifu once mentioned some Nethermancer who tracked a Mirage Realm, snuck into the Sanctum... and got mysteriously dumped right back at the entrance.\n\nHeh. Bet you anything that \"Nethermancer\" was him.\n\nSo this Mirage Realm was probably here in the Sanctum the whole time, not something Muyu created. Well, we're still inside the Sanctum, at least.\n\n...\n\nApart from the ground, this Mirage Realm roughly divides into three layers: the <ano=Human>Ren</ano> Realm, the <ano=Earth>Di</ano> Realm... and the one above them, which I guess should be called the \"<ano=Heaven>Tian</ano>Realm.\" Each layer's got its own Cloud Shuttles running. And there's this lightway hanging right before the whole fleet, the only way to move between layers.\n\nCould that lightway be our ticket out of here? Need to check.\n\n...\n\nIt's confirmed. Muyu still doesn't have full control over these Cloud Shuttles and Autopuppets. So he's basically squatting in this Mirage Realm at the end of the day.\n\nSure, he can somehow order the Autopuppets to attack.\n\nBut it's more like... he's hijacking the Cloud Shuttles' own defense systems.\n\nMostly he just rigged the mechanisms with this mist laced with Reverberations. That's how he got into the Sanctum in the first place. It's actually some kind of Disorienting Fog, and it spreads fast, corrupts fast. Any regular mechanism that touches it goes haywire real quick.\n\nStay sharp, {PlayerName}.",
+  "InfoDisplay_36050005_Text": "(There's messy handwriting crammed into the margins, seemingly added bit by bit over time.)\n\nShifu once mentioned some Nethermancer who tracked a Mirage Realm, snuck into the Sanctum... and got mysteriously dumped right back at the entrance.\n\nHeh. Bet you anything that \"Nethermancer\" was him.\n\nSo this Mirage Realm was probably here in the Sanctum the whole time, not something Muyu created. Well, we're still inside the Sanctum, at least.\n\n...\n\nApart from the ground, this Mirage Realm roughly divides into three layers: the <ano=Human>Ren</ano> Realm, the <ano=Earth>Di</ano> Realm... and the one above them, which I guess should be called the \"<ano=Heaven>Tian</ano> Realm.\" Each layer's got its own Cloud Shuttles running. And there's this lightway hanging right before the whole fleet, the only way to move between layers.\n\nCould that lightway be our ticket out of here? Need to check.\n\n...\n\nIt's confirmed. Muyu still doesn't have full control over these Cloud Shuttles and Autopuppets. So he's basically squatting in this Mirage Realm at the end of the day.\n\nSure, he can somehow order the Autopuppets to attack.\n\nBut it's more like... he's hijacking the Cloud Shuttles' own defense systems.\n\nMostly he just rigged the mechanisms with this mist laced with Reverberations. That's how he got into the Sanctum in the first place. It's actually some kind of Disorienting Fog, and it spreads fast, corrupts fast. Any regular mechanism that touches it goes haywire real quick.\n\nStay sharp, {PlayerName}.",
   "InfoDisplay_36050005_Title": "Scribbled Note I",
   "InfoDisplay_36050006_Text": "Now, let's talk about Muyu.\n\nOn the surface, he's a madman who won't shut up about his plans and ideals. But the guy's actually careful. Real cagey. He knows how to cover his real face or what he's really after.\n\nBack in Xuanfang Hold, he had almost everyone fooled. He used the Reverberations from the Fortress and Gorges War to mess with the Autopuppets, got them to turn on the Hold and tear the place apart. All of that just to test his methods and carve out a window to sneak his true body into the Sanctum. Yes, all that trouble, every piece set just so, only to slip into this Mirage. Nobody knows the full picture but him. Not even the Zhuojun Atelier's main branch got the real story.\n\nIf you and Paragon Qingxiao get to him first, don't let him talk his way around you.\n...\n\nGood thing I attached my Resonance Energy to that Qingfu pendant I gave you earlier.\n\nIf you run into something super weird along the way, it might just come in handy.\n\n...\n\nNot sure if you'll ever see this. Maybe it'll just be me facing Muyu inside this Mirage in the end. Guess I never said it outright. I came to make trouble for him too, same as you.\n\nGonna sniff out whatever scheme that bastard's cooking, then find my moment to end him.\n\nBut since he's got all those Autopuppets with him, I'll need a few cards up my sleeve.\n\nMy money's on you, great {PlayerName}.\n\nIf you found these messages, then we're not far apart.",
   "InfoDisplay_36050006_Title": "Scribbled Note II",
   "InfoDisplay_36050007_Text": "...\nOn Mt. Firmament, there dwells a Tacet Discord. Its form resembles a tiger, with golden eyes and a cyan face. Its back is covered in scales, and its long tail is tipped with spines. It is called the Lightstrider. Fierce by nature, it shuns company and claims the open wilds as its own. It fights with teeth and claws, its strength enough to shatter stone. When angered, it can transform its gleaming scales into projectiles, moving through the air as swiftly as a beam of light.\n\nWhen an ordinary person sees its radiance in the distance, they should fall silent and take a wide berth. On no account should they provoke it.\n\nIf caught in a narrow encounter with no way to retreat, one must still the heart and act according to the moment. When it lunges from above, meet it head‑on to break its momentum. If strength proves insufficient, seize the first chance to flee and avoid its edge. Above all, do not hesitate. A moment of doubt is a moment of ruin.",
   "InfoDisplay_36050007_Title": "Records of Huanglong Tacet Discord: Jinzhou",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000001_Text": "It still won't work. Even with Lady Hsin's techniques, the prototype burns through its energy far too fast, and its structure falls into an irreversible collapse of its own making...\nWhat am I to do... Have I taken the wrong direction entirely?\nNo, impossible. Jiening and I gave our lives to this. For her sake, I have to finish it.\n\n[A single line is written below. To your surprise, the hand is nothing like the writing above. It is your own, and it was clearly set down here a very long time ago.]\n\nFace the vase: forward, left, left, right.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000001_Title": "[A Hastily Written Note]",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000002_Text": "The Fifth Seal collected damaged tissues from victims to study the Evil Miasma's corrosion of the human face, leading to the blueprint for the Blight Rain protective mask. After the Second Seal crafted the prototype, the Fourth Seal replicated it into ten identical masks without sacrificing their performance, granting the Ten Seals the means to enter the Blight Rain and fight the Evil Miasma.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000002_Title": "Ten Seals Covenants' Masks",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000003_Text": "1. The mechanical parts requested by the Second and Eighth Seals have arrived. Remember to pick them up.\n \n 2. The Third and Seventh Seals went to patrol the outskirts of the city. If they aren't back in six hours, inform the Seal Master.\n \n 3. The Fourth Seal has been overusing her Forte for days and needs rest. (Send Sister Suoming to keep her company, that'll lift her spirits in no time!)\n \n 5. The Fifth and Sixth Seals went to the clinic together to tend to the patients.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37000003_Title": "First Seal's Journal",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010001_Text": "...It has been ██ days since the Formrenders first appeared, and at last we have found a way to relight the Moon Lanterns.\nThose faint glimmers scattered through the alleys—Luobin calls them <b>Nightlight Tokens</b>—carry some very peculiar frequency. <b>Burn them in the Moon Lanterns, and the darkness gives way.</b> They dull the Formrenders as well: the brighter the flame, the heavier and slower their movements. But lighting a Lantern also rouses their vigilance, so we must take the utmost care.\nWhere the glimmers come from, none of us knows. Faint as they are, one always rekindles somewhere just as the oil runs dry and the wick burns out. Whatever the truth of it, so long as we have the Nightlight Tokens, there is still hope. Jianwei believes it is a blessing bestowed by the Sentinel... But if it truly is a blessing, why has She never shown Herself?\n...Last night I heard the wind sweep down the corridor, and in my terror I snatched up a weapon and rushed outside, only to startle the neighbors. Then I remembered the Fortress and Gorges War ended long ago. My memory really has been failing me of late. Best to write it all down.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010001_Title": "[Scattered Note: Nightlight Tokens]",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010002_Text": "...Those who have seen it call it the Formrender. Blue of face, long of fang, it wears the shape of an Autopuppet, yet the air about it is foul. Its voice grates like a rusted blade scraping bone, and a red light sits in its eyes. It keeps to dark places, and loathes above all the joys of mortal men. At the sight of them it wakes to wrath, and in its wrath it devours that light.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010002_Title": "[Scattered Note: The Formrenders]",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010003_Text": "To my wife, Mingxi,\nI hope this letter finds you well. Your note and the dried fruit reached me safely, and I am in good health. There is no need to worry about me. Not a single piece was crushed on the way, and I confess I could not bring myself to share any with my colleagues; I ate them all myself. Every one was wonderfully sweet, and I was quite content. I only hope that next time you might spare a few more words for me.\nMatters at the Ministry have kept me busy of late, so this reply comes later than it should. Forgive me. I have picked out a hairpin for you, one of the styles now fashionable in the city, in a pattern I know you like. As for the reassignment, it is still under discussion, and my posting has not been decided. I mention it only so that it will not sit on your mind later.\nBy the time this reaches you, autumn will likely have set in. Remember to dress warmly, morning and night. Do not spend all your care on the children. Have a few new clothes made for yourself as well. Counting the days, I may be able to take leave around the time of the Waking Moon Festival. If the leave is granted, I will be home before dusk, and we will go to see the lanterns together.\nThere is more in my heart than this page can hold. Take good care of yourself.\nYours,\nGuilan",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010003_Title": "An Old, Yellowed Letter",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010004_Text": "A carefully preserved family photo, capturing an ordinary yet precious moment of happiness.",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010004_Title": "A Family Photo",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010005_Text": "To my wife, Mingxi,\nI hope this letter finds you well. The paperwork has piled high of late, and I have not written back in time. Forgive me for leaving you to worry. I am in good health.\nThe Tacet Discord Outbreaks along the border have grown worse, and there have been some transfers within the Ministry. One of them... concerns me, though it is still under discussion. If it is settled, <s>I am to be stationed in the Land of Xuanfang</s> and I will be even farther from you than I am now... As for where I am bound, and when I set out, I am not yet at liberty to write...\n(The letter breaks off here, leaving only a few blots of ink, as though the writer had held his brush poised for a long while and, in the end, set it down without going on.)",
+  "InfoDisplay_37010005_Title": "An Incomplete Letter",
   "InfoDisplay_70050063_Text": "A photo secretly taken by the Plushie Squad. They witnessed your ascending to the top.",
   "InfoDisplay_70050063_Tittle": "Above the Stars",
   "InfoDisplay_70050065_Text": "Completed a month before the Blessed Maiden's coronation, this portrait has invited much discussion within the halls of Avinoleum. What, exactly, is the Blessed Maiden contemplating? Some believe she is lost in fond memories of the past; others argue she reflects on weightier matters like faith. A few suggest her thoughts go to the future of Ragunna, or all of Rinascita itself.\n\nWhatever the truth, perhaps only the Maiden herself holds the answer.",
