-  "ItemInfo_80001090_BgDescription": "Made with fresh live fish from the Luo River, gently poached over a low flame and dressed in a traditional sweet-and-sour sauce. The finished dish gleams a glossy red, the flesh silver-white at every cut, delicate and tangy-sweet on the tongue. The recipe is an old one, and no shortage of variations have appeared over the years, but only the original may be called \"Mengzhou Fish in Vinegar.\"\nAt the Waking Moon Festival in Yuan Fortress long ago, Qingxiao once tasted this dish at the famed restaurant Yuan's Flavors. Lanterns filled the city that night; dragons and fishes of light danced above the crowds, and every face wore a smile. A century later, fewer and fewer can cook it the way it tasted back then. Qingxiao has tried her own hand at it, but never managed to bring back the taste she remembers.",
